# Domain 1: baseline build, upgrade plan v6.12.0, activation gating and node wiring.

[feature.1]
name = "baseline-build"
scope = "The paxd binary builds from main with the kernel library linked, a node build workflow gates every change, the plan table carries v6.12.0 in place of the v6.11 name with a handler that runs the folded SID work and five hooks (pointers, launchpad, pricefeed, perps, spot), the binary reports v6.12.0, the upgrade-info document has a fixed shape, the handler switches 0x1015 and 0x1017 to their v6.12.0 versions and serves 0x1020-0x1025 through one explicit live switch (0x1026 and 0x1027 stay gated with no code), the venue end-block and activation receipts are served through the receipt, log and bloom paths, and the new modules, precompiles, hooks, ante, gasless, sequencer and priority paths are wired into the node. Feature 1 uses waves 0, 2 and 3; it has no wave 1 task because nothing of the baseline waits on a wave 1 product."
requirements = ["1001", "1002", "1003", "1004", "1005", "1006", "1007", "1008", "1009", "1010", "1011", "1012"]
completion_task = "1.3.99"

[req.1001]
title = "paxd links the kernel library on every build path"
ac_1 = "The cgo host shim links liblayerx and the programs sandbox library through modules/lxphost/host.go:7 and includes the generated headers through modules/lxphost/host.go:6; every file of the shim is built only with cgo (modules/lxphost/host.go:1), and precompiles/layerxexchange/errors.go:7 places the shim in the dependency graph of paxd."
ac_2 = "A make target builds liblayerx (Makefile:46, Makefile:216-218), the generated checkpoint settlement header (Makefile:28, Makefile:232-235) and the release sandbox library (Makefile:3406, Makefile:3423-3425) before any Go build of paxd; required change: today no target orders the native libraries before the chain build (Makefile:3141-3142 forwards build to chain.mk without them)."
ac_3 = "The shim searches programs/target/release before `programs/target/debug`, so a release build of the sandbox library (Makefile:3406) satisfies the link without a debug build; required change at modules/lxphost/host.go:7."
ac_4 = "make test-lxphost builds the native libraries, then runs go test ./modules/lxphost/..., and TestHostLinksKernel (modules/lxphost/host_test.go:210) passes."
ac_5 = "make paxd-build produces build/paxd through the chain build (chain.mk:185-186) with the native libraries in place, and GOPROXY=off holds for the Go step as in paxeer-build (Makefile:3141-3142)."

[req.1002]
title = "A node build workflow gates every change to the node"
ac_1 = "A workflow .github/workflows/node-build.yml runs on push to main and on pull requests that touch node, modules, precompiles, engine, sdk, daemon, src, include, programs, Makefile or chain.mk; a new workflow file is enabled by default, unlike the cross-architecture build workflow whose build step (.github/workflows/paxeer-cross-arch-build.yml:176-186) is disabled in the repository Actions settings."
ac_2 = "Every job routes runs-on through the same expression as .github/workflows/ci.yml:22, so scripts/ci/runner-routing-check.sh accepts the file."
ac_3 = "The jobs are native-libs (make paxd-native-libs), paxd (make paxd-build then make paxd-version-check), lxphost (make test-lxphost) and node-tests (go test ./node/... ./modules/layerxcustody/...)."
ac_4 = "A final job node-build-gate needs every other job and fails when any of them did not succeed, so a required check names one job."

[req.1003]
title = "The plan table carries v6.12.0 and no longer carries v6.11"
ac_1 = "V611Upgrade (node/upgrades.go:104-112) and its handler registration (node/upgrades.go:204-206) are removed, per decision.1."
ac_2 = "node/upgrades_v6120.go declares const V6120Upgrade = \"v6.12.0\" (task 1.0.3); the release check greps for that declaration, not for the bare plan string, because GovernanceActivationUpgrade (modules/layerxcustody/types/governance_activation.go:5) carries the same string and would satisfy the generic grep of .github/workflows/paxeer-release-check.yml:45-49 before the plan exists (required change, task 8.4.4)."
ac_3 = "knownUpgradePlans (node/upgrades.go:532-534) returns ActivationUpgrade, V610Upgrade, V6120Upgrade, MergeUpgrade in that order."
ac_4 = "RegisterUpgradeHandlers (node/upgrades.go:130-210) registers app.runV6120Upgrade under V6120Upgrade next to the v6.10 registration (node/upgrades.go:203)."
ac_5 = "The custody governance gate constant GovernanceActivationUpgrade (modules/layerxcustody/types/governance_activation.go:5) carries \"v6.12.0\", so GovernanceExecutionActive (modules/layerxcustody/keeper/keeper.go:38-46) opens at the v6.12.0 height."
ac_6 = "The governance activation test TestCustodyGovernanceV611ActivationBoundaries (node/upgrades_v611_test.go:26) is retargeted to V6120Upgrade with the same height boundaries."

[req.1004]
title = "The v6.12.0 handler runs the folded SID work and the five hooks, then serves the v6.12.0 precompile set"
ac_1 = "runV6120Upgrade runs RunMigrations, then moveSidioraMintAuthority (node/upgrades_v611.go:115-134), then migrateSIDHolders (node/upgrades_v611.go:141), in the order runV611Upgrade uses today (node/upgrades_v611.go:98-110)."
ac_2 = "migrateSIDHolders keeps its rules: a chain that already migrated is skipped (node/upgrades_v611.go:142), the slot value wins over the listed balance (node/upgrades_v611.go:152-157), and a holder whose slot reads zero mints nothing (node/upgrades_v611.go:158-160); the holder list node/testdata/sid-holders.json (node/upgrades_v611.go:19-22) is a release input."
ac_3 = "After the folded steps the handler calls, in this order, the pointers hook (task 1.2.4), launchpad MigrateV6120(ctx, k, evm), pricefeed InitV6120(ctx, k), perps SeedV6120(ctx, k) and spot InitV6120(ctx, k), so the uhpx and SID pointers exist before the launchpad and spot hooks read them and the price feed is initialised before the perpetuals markets that read it are seeded."
ac_4 = "A hook error aborts the plan: the handler returns \"upgrade v6.12.0: <hook>: <error>\" and the version map is not returned, so the upgrade keeper does not record a done height."
ac_5 = "While a hook is unbound the handler returns \"upgrade v6.12.0: hook <name> is not bound\" before any state is written, so the plan cannot apply partially."
ac_6 = "runV611Upgrade (node/upgrades_v611.go:98-110) is deleted; the SID helpers it calls stay in node/upgrades_v611.go."
ac_7 = "The handler ends by setting the v6.12.0 precompile set live itself, app.setV6120Live(true), as runActivationUpgrade calls setXWebPrecompile(true) (node/upgrades.go:304-318); it reads no done height, because the upgrade keeper runs the handler first and records the done height after it returns (sdk/x/upgrade/keeper/keeper.go:369-395)."
ac_8 = "The SID work of the v6.11 plan ships inside v6.12.0: only the plan name v6.11 is dropped (decision.1), so the mint authority move and the holder migration run exactly once, at the v6.12.0 height."
ac_9 = "The hook table is the App field v6120HookTable, built by bindV6120Hooks in the application constructor (task 1.3.100); tests in package node replace the field with hooks that return nil, so the custody and SID tests run the handler on a test application without the venue state."

[req.1005]
title = "The binary reports version v6.12.0"
ac_1 = "paxd version prints version.Version (sdk/version/command.go:15-24, sdk/version/version.go:26-34), which the build sets through -X github.com/Sidiora-Labs/Paxeer-X-Network/sdk/version.Version (chain.mk:65-69)."
ac_2 = "make paxd-build passes LDFLAGS carrying -X github.com/Sidiora-Labs/Paxeer-X-Network/sdk/version.Version set from the version key of tools/release/version.json (tools/release/version.json:2), appended to the chain ldflags (chain.mk:80), so the CI build and the release build (tools/release/build-paxd.sh:19) read one source."
ac_3 = "make paxd-version-check runs build/paxd version and fails unless the output equals the version key of tools/release/version.json; with that key at v6.12.0 the output is v6.12.0."
ac_4 = "The application version recorded by the base app comes from the same variable (node/app.go:593), so the node info and the CLI agree."

[req.1006]
title = "The upgrade-info document has a fixed shape"
ac_1 = "The document is upgrade-info.json (sdk/x/upgrade/keeper/keeper.go:28-29) under <home>/data (sdk/x/upgrade/keeper/keeper.go:434-442), written with mode 0600 (sdk/x/upgrade/keeper/keeper.go:414-431)."
ac_2 = "Its keys are name, height and the optional info (sdk/x/upgrade/keeper/keeper.go:479-486; sdk/store/types/store.go:56-59); for this release name is \"v6.12.0\" and height is the halt height plus one."
ac_3 = "A missing document means no upgrade (sdk/x/upgrade/keeper/keeper.go:453-476), and applyNamedUpgrade (node/upgrades.go:574-604) applies v6.12.0 only in the block whose height equals the document height and only when the plan is still pending (node/upgrades.go:594)."
ac_4 = "A test writes the document through DumpUpgradeInfoToDisk (sdk/x/upgrade/keeper/keeper.go:406-408), as writeV610UpgradeInfo does (node/upgrades_v610_test.go:20-27), reads it back and asserts exactly {\"name\":\"v6.12.0\",\"height\":<H+1>}."

[req.1007]
title = "The plan gates the new precompiles and switches 0x1015 and 0x1017 explicitly"
ac_1 = "A second activation entry v6120PrecompileGate names Upgrade V6120Upgrade with 0x1020 serving the pricefeed module and 0x1021-0x1025 serving the spot module, passed to SetCustomPrecompileActivation (modules/evm/keeper/keeper.go:207-241) beside activationPrecompileGate (node/upgrades.go:489-503); 0x1026 and 0x1027 carry no code at any height, so eth_getCode returns 0x for them before and after the done height."
ac_2 = "0x1015 and 0x1017 stay only in activationPrecompileGate (node/upgrades.go:496), because SetCustomPrecompileActivation refuses two entries naming one address (modules/evm/keeper/keeper.go:230-233); their v6.12.0 versions are selected by the live switch of ac_4, not by an activation entry."
ac_3 = "0x1015 is served by exchangeVersionSwitch(perps, legacy, live) and 0x1017 by launchpadVersionSwitch(g2, g1, live), each a putils.VersionedPrecompiles in the pattern of precompiles/p256/setup.go:15-24: with live true the map is {LatestUpgrade: new, ActivationUpgrade: legacy, V6120Upgrade: new}; with live false it is {LatestUpgrade: legacy, ActivationUpgrade: legacy}. The legacy value of 0x1015 is the unchanged v6.9 exchange contract of precompiles/layerxexchange NewPrecompile (precompiles/layerxexchange/layerxexchange.go:140); the legacy value of 0x1017 is the current launchpad contract kept by the launchpad domain under precompiles/launchpad/legacy/v610. This is the only version mechanism for the two addresses (decision.10)."
ac_4 = "Ordinary execution serves versioned[LatestUpgrade] (modules/evm/keeper/keeper.go:171-187), and LatestUpgrade is the last line of node/tags, today v6.8 (node/upgrades.go:47-55); v6.12.0 is a named plan with no node/tags entry, so LatestUpgrade does not move. The App field v6120Live selects the set: the handler sets it through setV6120Live(true) (req 1.4 ac_7); at load (after LoadLatestVersion, beside refreshXWebPrecompile at node/app.go:1188) and in InitChainer (node/app.go:1466) it is restored from GetDoneHeight(ctx, V6120Upgrade) > 0, the rule xwebLive uses outside the handler (node/upgrades.go:253-261). setXWebPrecompile (node/upgrades.go:276-282) and RefreshPrecompiles (node/upgrades.go:271) build the set through v6120PrecompileSet(all, xwebLive, v6120Live), so a restarted node and a running node serve one set at H1+1. Tracing picks the version by done height through GetCustomPrecompilesVersions (modules/evm/keeper/keeper.go:356-385): ActivationUpgrade (legacy) below the v6.12.0 done height and V6120Upgrade (new) at and above it."
ac_5 = "A call to 0x1020-0x1025 before the v6.12.0 done height is not served: the address behaves as an account with no code, as for every address withheld by customPrecompileReached (modules/evm/keeper/keeper.go:333-350)."
ac_6 = "The giga executor hands every v6.12.0 address to the ordinary path: gigaCustomPrecompiles (node/app.go:2564-2569) returns, at and above gigaLatePrecompileHeight (node/app.go:2559), gigaV6120FailFast, which is AllCustomPrecompilesFailFastLate (engine/executor/precompiles/failfast.go:128, already holding 0x1015 and 0x1017 through LateFailFastPrecompileAddresses at engine/executor/precompiles/failfast.go:116-123) plus 0x1020-0x1025 mapped to FailFastSingleton (engine/executor/precompiles/failfast.go:101); a giga call to any of them fails fast and the ordinary EVM re-executes it with the version the live switch selects. 0x1026 and 0x1027 carry no code and are not in the map."

[req.1008]
title = "The plan mounts the new module stores"
ac_1 = "v6120StoreUpgrades adds the store keys of modules/perps, modules/spot and modules/pricefeed and deletes and renames none, in the shape of activationStoreUpgrades (node/upgrades.go:398-402); the three names are added to kvStoreKeyNames (node/app.go:313-330) and to MemIAVLStoreKeys (storage/common/keys/store_keys.go:47) with their constants beside storage/common/keys/store_keys.go:30-44, so TestKVStoreKeyNamesMatchMemIAVLStoreKeys holds and the composite store accepts the new stores."
ac_2 = "layerxStoreUpgrades (node/app.go:1407-1421) returns v6120StoreUpgrades for V6120Upgrade, so SetStoreUpgradeHandlers (node/app.go:1321-1404) mounts the stores at the plan height through its layerx branch (node/app.go:1400-1403)."
ac_3 = "applyNamedUpgrade calls unmountedPlanStores(V6120Upgrade) before ApplyUpgrade runs the handler and panics with the plan and store names when one of the three stores is not mounted, as it refuses the activation plan (node/upgrades.go:597-600, node/upgrades.go:633-644), so RunMigrations never reaches an unmounted store."
ac_4 = "The existing TestKVStoreKeyNamesMatchMemIAVLStoreKeys (node/store_keys_test.go:15) passes with the three new store names: kvStoreKeyNames and MemIAVLStoreKeys agree."

[req.1009]
title = "The new modules, precompiles and hooks are wired and the plan applies to a halt-height export"
ac_1 = "ModuleBasics (node/app.go:268-279), the store keys (node/app.go:318-330), the keeper fields (node/app.go:476-482), keeper construction (node/app.go:802-811), the module manager (node/app.go:994-1003), SetOrderInitGenesis (node/app.go:1052-1083) and SetOrderMidBlockers (node/app.go:1043-1045, oracle then pricefeed) carry perps, spot and pricefeed beside launchpad (node/app.go:275, node/app.go:326, node/app.go:480, node/app.go:806-807, node/app.go:1000)."
ac_2 = "The custom precompile set built at node/app.go:961-965 adds the 0x1015 entry through exchangeVersionSwitch, the 0x1017 entry through launchpadVersionSwitch, precompiles/pricefeed NewPrecompile at 0x1020 and every entry of the (map, error) result of precompiles/spot NewPrecompileSet at 0x1021-0x1025 to the result of GetCustomPrecompiles (precompiles/setup.go:160-201); the spot set is registered only here, never in precompiles/setup.go, so no address is registered twice."
ac_3 = "PrecompileKeepers (node/precompiles.go:17-41) and NewPrecompileKeepers (node/precompiles.go:43-69) carry the perps, spot and pricefeed keepers behind the accessors PerpsK(), SpotK() and PriceFeedK(), and precompiles/utils/expected_keepers.go declares PerpsKeepers, SpotKeepers and PriceFeedKeepers beside XWebKeepers (precompiles/utils/expected_keepers.go:57-61), which the precompile packages type-assert."
ac_4 = "The v6.12.0 hook table binds the pointers hook of task 1.2.4, modules/launchpad/keeper MigrateV6120, modules/pricefeed/keeper InitV6120, modules/perps/keeper SeedV6120 and modules/spot/keeper InitV6120, so no hook reports \"is not bound\"."
ac_5 = "TestV6120AppliesThePlanOnTheHaltExport seeds a test application from node/testdata/v6120-halt-export.json, writes the upgrade-info document for height H+1, runs BeginBlock at H+1 (node/abci.go:59) and asserts the v6.12.0 done height H+1, the five hooks' state, 0x1015 serving the perps version and 0x1017 the G2 version, 0x1020-0x1025 served, eth_getCode 0x at 0x1026 and 0x1027, and a call to 0x1015 executed in the same process at H+2 returning the perps result."
ac_6 = "Module accounts follow the bank rule that every maccPerms address is a blocked receiver unless it is in allowedReceivingModAcc (node/app.go:3465): spot is added to maccPerms (node/app.go:282-300) with {Minter, Burner}, the keeper restricting mint and burn to spot/share/* denoms, and to allowedReceivingModAcc (node/app.go:304-306), so users can send uhpx and SID to it; perps, launchpad and pricefeed get no maccPerms entry and no mint right (the comment of node/app.go:296-299 applies), and nothing mints USDL, which stays the existing ERC20 (decision.3)."
ac_7 = "A MsgSubmitPrices tx is gasless and prioritised on every path: IsTxGasless (node/antedecorators/gasless.go:73-104) takes the pricefeed keeper and dispatches pricefeed.SubmissionIsGasless; every caller passes it (node/app.go:1704, node/app.go:1978, node/app.go:3312, node/ante/cosmos_checktx.go:85, node/ante/cosmos_delivertx.go:37, node/antedecorators/gasless.go:33, node/sequencer/fee.go:71, node/sequencer/layers.go:291); couldBeGaslessTransaction (node/app.go:3403), the sequencer couldBeGasless (node/sequencer/layers.go:329) and isExpectedGaslessMetricsError (node/app.go:3387) know the message; CheckTxKeepers and DeliverTxKeepers (node/legacyabci/check_tx.go:32-41, node/legacyabci/deliver_tx.go:28-36) carry the pricefeed keeper into CosmosCheckTxAnte and CosmosDeliverTxAnte, which call pricefeed.CheckSubmission after IsTxGasless; CosmosStatelessChecks (node/ante/cosmos_checktx.go:136) applies types.CheckSubmissionAlone; CheckMessage (node/ante/cosmos_checktx.go:537) calls pricefeed.MarkSubmission; isOracleTx (node/prioritizer.go:185, node/antedecorators/priority.go:45), DecoratePriority (node/ante/cosmos_checktx.go:118, node/ante/cosmos_checktx.go:335) and IsTxPrioritized (utils/prioritized_txs.go:9) treat types.IsSubmissionTx as an oracle tx."
ac_8 = "EndBlockKeepers (node/legacyabci/end_block.go:15-20) carries the perps and spot keepers and a func field V6120Live, set in the app literal (node/app.go:1017) to read app.v6120Live; EndBlock calls perps then spot after oracle.EndBlocker and before EvmKeeper.EndBlock (node/legacyabci/end_block.go:22-28) only while V6120Live returns true, so blocks below H1, whose stores are not mounted, never reach the venue end-blockers."

[req.1010]
title = "The node domain passes its package test set once"
ac_1 = "make test-paxd-domain runs make test-lxphost and go test ./node/... ./modules/layerxcustody/... ./modules/evm/keeper/... ./rpc/... once against the wired tree and exits 0."
ac_2 = "The target depends on paxd-native-libs, so it runs on a clean checkout without a prior build."

[req.1011]
title = "The v6.12.0 handler creates the uhpx and SID native pointers first"
ac_1 = "The first hook, named pointers, writes bank metadata for uhpx (BaseDenom, modules/evm/keeper/params.go:22) with exponent 6 when the denom has none, and fails with \"upgrade v6.12.0: pointers: uhpx exponent <n>, want 6\" when existing metadata carries another exponent."
ac_2 = "For SID it reads the metadata of layerxbridgetypes.SidioraDenom() (modules/layerxbridge/types/keys.go:53-59), which EnsureSidioraDenom writes with SidioraDecimals 6 (modules/layerxbridge/keeper/sidiora.go:51-60, modules/layerxbridge/types/keys.go:18), and fails when it is absent or its exponent is not 6."
ac_3 = "For each of the two denoms it keeps an existing native pointer (GetERC20NativePointer, modules/evm/keeper/pointer.go:46) and otherwise deploys one through RunWithOneOffEVMInstance and UpsertERCNativePointer (modules/evm/keeper/pointer_upgrade.go:17, modules/evm/keeper/pointer_upgrade.go:49) with name, symbol and decimals derived from the metadata as precompiles/pointer/pointer.go:99-131 derives them, the pattern of modules/evm/gov.go:54-66."
ac_4 = "USDL gets no pointer and no bank denom: it stays the existing ERC20 contract 0x85FcD13735F4309833A503EE804ea32395851479 (contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:14, 6 decimals at contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:16)."
ac_5 = "Running the hook a second time on the same state writes nothing and returns nil, and the two pointer addresses are read back through getNativePointer of the pointer view precompile 0x100A (precompiles/pointerview/pointerview.go:18, precompiles/pointerview/pointerview.go:24) and checked by tools/release/fleet_check.py (task 8.4.10)."

[req.1012]
title = "The venue end-block and activation receipts are served through the receipt, log and bloom paths"
ac_1 = "Each synthetic receipt has a fixed hash: perps keccak256(\"perps-endblock\" || height), spot keccak256(\"spot-endblock\" || height) and activation keccak256(\"v6120-activation\" || height), with height as 8 bytes big-endian; modules/evm/keeper/synthetic_receipts.go exports SyntheticReceiptHash(kind, height) for the kinds SyntheticReceiptPerps (1), SyntheticReceiptSpot (2) and SyntheticReceiptActivation (3)."
ac_2 = "Venue code writes its logs through SyntheticReceiptContext(ctx, kind), which sets ctx.WithTxSum(hash).WithTxIndex(provisional) before CallEVM (modules/evm/keeper/evm.go:81-150), so CallEVM merges every log of one kind and one block into one receipt (modules/evm/keeper/evm.go:127-137) instead of writing at the zero TxSum and index 0 of a module context; the provisional index is math.MaxUint32 - 3 + kind, outside every real index, so AppendToEvmTxDeferredInfo never overwrites a real transaction's deferred info and GetAllEVMTxDeferredInfo (modules/evm/keeper/deferred.go:13) ignores it; the surplus of such a call is zero because the gas price is zero (modules/evm/keeper/evm.go:104-106)."
ac_3 = "flushTransientReceipts (modules/evm/keeper/receipt.go:142) rewrites TransactionIndex of the three receipts and of their logs to N + kind - 1, where N is the number of transactions of the block (len of txResults, set at node/app.go:2236): perps is the highest real index + 1, spot + 2, activation + 3; a kind with no logs in the block has no receipt."
ac_4 = "The EVM EndBlock bloom step (modules/evm/keeper/abci.go:190-214) adds the bloom of each synthetic receipt of the height to allBlooms and to evmOnlyBlooms, so SetBlockBloom and SetEvmOnlyBlockBloom cover the venue logs and a bloom-filtered eth_getLogs or pax_getLogs finds them."
ac_5 = "getTxHashesFromBlock (rpc/utils.go:533-553) appends, after the block's transactions, the synthetic hashes of the height whose receipt exists, in kind order, for both the eth and the pax namespaces; the shell filter of rpc/utils.go:454 and shouldIncludeSynthetic (rpc/utils.go:521-526) apply only to wasm shell receipts, not to these hashes."
ac_6 = "eth_getLogs and pax_getLogs (rpc/filter.go normalizeRangeQueryLogs at :1507, collectLogs at :1598), eth_getBlockReceipts (rpc/block.go:344) and eth_getTransactionReceipt (rpc/tx.go:110) return the synthetic receipts and their logs with the hash, TransactionIndex and log indices of ac_1 and ac_3; block bodies (rpc/block.go:493, rpc/block.go:703) do not list them as transactions; debug tracing treats them as untraceable (isReceiptUntraceable, rpc/utils.go:582)."
ac_7 = "Data services key rows by (block, tx_index, log_index, sub) and never by the receipt's from address, so the synthetic receipts index without a sender."

