[feature.2]
name = "launchpad"
scope = "The launchpad of Paxeer X Network at 0x1017 rebuilt to the exact interface of the Launch-x contracts of the manifest-active generation 2, with USDL kept as the ERC20 contract and held in custody at the launchpad module EVM address through nested ERC20 calls, the Treasury served over a keeper ledger, opticals, ERC721 fee rights and the deployed SidioraERC20 pool tokens, and the v6.12.0 migration of every generation 1 and generation 2 pool into generation 2 surfaces that serve every generation."
requirements = ["2001", "2002", "2003", "2004", "2005", "2006", "2007", "2008", "2009", "2010", "2011", "2012", "2013", "2014", "2015", "2016", "2017", "2018", "2019", "2020", "2021", "2022", "2023", "2024", "2025", "2026", "2027", "2028", "2029", "2030", "2031", "2032", "2033", "2034", "2035", "2036", "2037", "2038", "2039", "2040"]
completion_task = "2.3.99"

[req.2001]
title = "The interface is frozen as one ABI file per contract role with a golden selector file"
ac_1 = "precompiles/launchpad/abi/ holds the compiled ABI of eleven role files copied from the Launch-x build at c5eb7c7 (the sources of Launch-x:contracts/contracts): the ten served roles SidioraPool, SidioraFactory, SidioraNFT, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, ProtocolConfig and Treasury (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:13), and SidioraERC20, which is not served but encodes the nested calls the precompile makes to pool-token contracts; each file is loaded with MustGetABI (precompiles/common/precompiles.go:449) through the embed.FS of precompiles/launchpad/launchpad.go:94."
ac_2 = "precompiles/launchpad/testdata/abi_golden.txt lists one line per function (role, signature, 4-byte selector), per event (role, signature, topic0) and per distinct custom error (role, signature, selector), each error written once per role even where the artifact lists it twice: 549 lines for SidioraPool, SidioraFactory, SidioraERC20, SidioraNFT, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, ProtocolConfig and the twelve EventEmitter launchpad events, 44 lines for Treasury (17 functions, 8 events, 19 errors) and 2 lines for the chain-defined errors AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(address,bytes32) 0xe2517d3f and Retired(address) 0xda9d2e31, 595 lines in all; any change to a role file that alters a line fails the test."
ac_3 = "precompiles/launchpad/abi.json becomes the ABI of direct calls to 0x1017: the union of the Router, SidioraFactory, Quoter, PoolRegistry, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator and ProtocolConfig functions taken in that order with the first role winning a shared signature (113 distinct selectors, the 21 shared signatures listed in contracts/launchpad.md section 3), plus the twelve EventEmitter launchpad events; the current abi.json and Launchpad.sol (precompiles/launchpad/launchpad.go:94) are copied to precompiles/launchpad/legacy/v610 by task 2.0.7 before they change."
ac_4 = "Two signatures with one selector never appear in one role or at 0x1017; the golden test asserts the selector set of each role and of 0x1017 has no duplicate."

[req.2002]
title = "Contract addresses become surfaces that forward to 0x1017 with the caller appended"
ac_1 = "MigrateV6120 replaces the runtime code at every pool address of generations 1 and 2, at the generation 2 fee-right collection 0xe8Dc…409B (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:58) and at the generation 2 SidioraFactory, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry and ProtocolConfig addresses (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:16-51, Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:65) and the generation 2 Treasury address read from SidioraFactory slot 6 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:30) and recorded in modules/launchpad/keeper/testdata/v6120/layout.json, with the 41-byte surface runtime 0x363d3d373360601b36523d3d601436013d3d6110175af13d600060003e6024573d6000fd5b3d6000f3, written with SetCode (modules/evm/keeper/code.go:23); the runtime copies calldata, appends CALLER and CALLs 0x1017 with all gas, returning or reverting with the callee data; pool-token contracts and USDL keep their code, and the generation 1 role addresses receive the retirement surface of requirement 2.36."
ac_2 = "The precompile treats the last 20 bytes of calldata as the original caller only when its own caller is a registered surface address (a keeper set written by MigrateV6120 and by market creation under a new prefix beside those of modules/launchpad/types/keys.go:36-48); for any other caller the calldata is decoded whole and the caller is the EVM caller, so no account can claim another caller by appending bytes."
ac_3 = "A call arriving from a surface selects the role ABI of that surface (pool, the generation 2 collection, or the generation 2 role of the address), so the same selector resolves per role; the generation 2 role surfaces serve the markets of every generation, migrated generation 1 pools included; direct calls to 0x1017 resolve through abi.json in the order Router, SidioraFactory, Quoter, PoolRegistry, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, ProtocolConfig."
ac_4 = "Delegatecall into 0x1017 reverts and a write under staticcall reverts, as precompiles/launchpad/launchpad.go:232 does today; a view selector under staticcall is served; value attached to any call reverts, matching ValidateNonPayable (precompiles/common/precompiles.go:374) and the non-payable functions of the contracts (the only payable function, upgradeToAndCall, reverts for every caller)."
ac_5 = "An unknown selector at a surface or at 0x1017 reverts with empty revert data, as a contract without a fallback does; the registered surface set is exported and imported by genesis (modules/launchpad/keeper/genesis.go:53)."

[req.2003]
title = "The SidioraPool surface serves every SidioraPool function"
ac_1 = "`PAUSER_ROLE()` (selector 0xe63ab1e9, view, returns `(bytes32)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/Pausable.sol:7 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the value the contract returned at the halt height for migrated state and the value of the launchpad keeper state afterwards, with identical ABI encoding."
ac_2 = "`SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL()` (selector 0x6d2beef1, view, returns `(uint256)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:80 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the value the contract returned at the halt height for migrated state and the value of the launchpad keeper state afterwards, with identical ABI encoding."
ac_3 = "`SNAPSHOT_MIN_VOLUME_BPS()` (selector 0x923795a3, view, returns `(uint256)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:81 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the value the contract returned at the halt height for migrated state and the value of the launchpad keeper state afterwards, with identical ABI encoding."
ac_4 = "`acceptGuardian()` (selector 0xa5f31d61, nonpayable, returns `()`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:314 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade with the contract behaviour of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:314: same preconditions, same state effects in the launchpad keeper, same return encoding, same logs and the same custom-error revert data."
ac_5 = "`accumulatedTokenFees()` (selector 0x1e5a0998, view, returns `(uint256)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:72 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the value the contract returned at the halt height for migrated state and the value of the launchpad keeper state afterwards, with identical ABI encoding."
ac_6 = "`accumulatedUsdlFees()` (selector 0x61f63bf5, view, returns `(uint256)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:71 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the value the contract returned at the halt height for migrated state and the value of the launchpad keeper state afterwards, with identical ABI encoding."
ac_7 = "`creationTimestamp()` (selector 0xb3311086, view, returns `(uint256)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:64 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the value the contract returned at the halt height for migrated state and the value of the launchpad keeper state afterwards, with identical ABI encoding."
ac_8 = "`cumulativeBuyUsdlVolume()` (selector 0x1aa6f435, view, returns `(uint256)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:78 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the value the contract returned at the halt height for migrated state and the value of the launchpad keeper state afterwards, with identical ABI encoding."
ac_9 = "`cumulativeSellUsdlVolume()` (selector 0x00a8b4fe, view, returns `(uint256)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:79 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the value the contract returned at the halt height for migrated state and the value of the launchpad keeper state afterwards, with identical ABI encoding."
ac_10 = "`cumulativeVolume()` (selector 0xf4dd4156, view, returns `(uint256)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:65 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the value the contract returned at the halt height for migrated state and the value of the launchpad keeper state afterwards, with identical ABI encoding."
ac_11 = "`currentFeeBps()` (selector 0x975f8f46, view, returns `(uint256)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:404 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the value the contract returned at the halt height for migrated state and the value of the launchpad keeper state afterwards, with identical ABI encoding."
ac_12 = "`emergencyPaused()` (selector 0x27c830a9, view, returns `(bool)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/Pausable.sol:10 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the value the contract returned at the halt height for migrated state and the value of the launchpad keeper state afterwards, with identical ABI encoding."
ac_13 = "`eventEmitter()` (selector 0x9ff78c30, view, returns `(address)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:57 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the generation 2 EventEmitter address 0x622E…3EF6 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:9) for every pool, the value MigrateV6120 writes into every market record and market creation writes for new markets (ruling 5), with identical ABI encoding."
ac_14 = "`factory()` (selector 0xc45a0155, view, returns `(address)`) declared at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:75 is served at every pool address of generations 1 and 2 and every pool created after the upgrade and returns the generation 2 SidioraFactory address 0x3993…8830 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:37) for every pool, the value MigrateV6120 writes into every market record and market creation writes for new markets (ruling 5), with identical ABI encoding."
