[req.2013]
title = "Access-control and upgrade functions answer from the migrated role table and administration moves to governance"
ac_1 = "`DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE()` (selector 0xa217fddf) of SidioraFactory, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, ProtocolConfig, SidioraNFT and Treasury at every generation 2 surface address of those roles and at 0x1017 returns 0x00 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/AccessControl.sol:9)."
ac_2 = "`getRoleAdmin(bytes32)` (selector 0x248a9ca3) of SidioraFactory, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, ProtocolConfig, SidioraNFT and Treasury at every generation 2 surface address of those roles and at 0x1017 answers from the migrated role table (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/AccessControl.sol:53)."
ac_3 = "`grantRole(bytes32,address)` (selector 0x2f2ff15d) of SidioraFactory, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, ProtocolConfig, SidioraNFT and Treasury at every generation 2 surface address of those roles and at 0x1017 reverts with `AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(address,bytes32)` (0xe2517d3f) carrying the caller and 0x00 for every caller (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/AccessControl.sol:58, ruling 7); grants run through MsgUpdateParams (requirement 2.40)."
ac_4 = "`hasRole(bytes32,address)` (selector 0x91d14854) of SidioraFactory, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, ProtocolConfig, SidioraNFT and Treasury at every generation 2 surface address of those roles and at 0x1017 answers from the migrated role table (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/AccessControl.sol:48); hasRole(0x00, any) is false after the upgrade, and role-gated functions of non-admin roles keep reverting MissingRole(account, role) (0x0161a64a, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/AccessControl.sol:73)."
ac_5 = "`proxiableUUID()` (selector 0x52d1902d) of SidioraFactory, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, ProtocolConfig, SidioraNFT and Treasury at every generation 2 surface address of those roles and at 0x1017 returns the revert data the proxy address returned at the halt height (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/UUPSUpgradeable.sol:41), since notDelegated refuses a call through the proxy."
ac_6 = "`registeredDefaultAdminCount()` (selector 0xc0cb71b6) of SidioraFactory, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, ProtocolConfig, SidioraNFT and Treasury at every generation 2 surface address of those roles and at 0x1017 returns 0 after the upgrade, since DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE is not migrated (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/AccessControl.sol:32)."
ac_7 = "`renounceRole(bytes32,address)` (selector 0x36568abe) of SidioraFactory, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, ProtocolConfig, SidioraNFT and Treasury at every generation 2 surface address of those roles and at 0x1017 is served as Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/AccessControl.sol:68-71 is: a callerConfirmation other than the caller reverts MissingRole(caller, role) (0x0161a64a), otherwise the caller loses the role and RoleRevoked is emitted at the surface."
ac_8 = "`revokeRole(bytes32,address)` (selector 0xd547741f) of SidioraFactory, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, ProtocolConfig, SidioraNFT and Treasury at every generation 2 surface address of those roles and at 0x1017 reverts with `AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(address,bytes32)` (0xe2517d3f) carrying the caller and 0x00 for every caller (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/AccessControl.sol:63, ruling 7); revokes run through MsgUpdateParams (requirement 2.40)."
ac_9 = "`upgradeToAndCall(address,bytes)` (selector 0x4f1ef286) of SidioraFactory, Router, Quoter, FeesRouter, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, ProtocolConfig, SidioraNFT and Treasury at every generation 2 surface address of those roles and at 0x1017 reverts with `AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(address,bytes32)` (0xe2517d3f) carrying the caller and 0x00, and a value-carrying call reverts first on the value check of the precompile (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/UUPSUpgradeable.sol:48, precompiles/common/precompiles.go:374)."

