[req.2017]
title = "Optical hooks are called with the contract callers and flags"
ac_1 = "The precompile calls `getFlags()` (selector 0x6cc7149d, implemented at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/presets/LaunchpadOptical.sol:151) on the market optical through evm.Call with caller the pool address, at the point of the contract flow Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:179, only when the optical flags carry every flag (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/libraries/BitFlag.sol:16); the optical code stays deployed unchanged and its sender checks pass (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/BaseOptical.sol:86)."
ac_2 = "The precompile calls `beforeSwap(address,address,bool,uint256)` (selector 0xae7e71d9, implemented at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/presets/LaunchpadOptical.sol:159) on the market optical through evm.Call with caller the pool address, at the point of the contract flow Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:188, only when the optical flags carry BEFORE_SWAP (1) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/libraries/BitFlag.sol:16); the optical code stays deployed unchanged and its sender checks pass (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/BaseOptical.sol:86)."
ac_3 = "The precompile calls `afterSwap(address,address,bool,uint256,uint256)` (selector 0xf74c1c1a, implemented at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/presets/LaunchpadOptical.sol:172) on the market optical through evm.Call with caller the pool address, at the point of the contract flow Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:262, only when the optical flags carry AFTER_SWAP (2) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/libraries/BitFlag.sol:16); the optical code stays deployed unchanged and its sender checks pass (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/BaseOptical.sol:86)."
ac_4 = "The precompile calls `beforeFeeDistribution(address,uint256)` (selector 0xf80d2cc7, implemented at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/presets/LaunchpadOptical.sol:208) on the market optical through evm.Call with caller the generation 2 FeeAccumulator address 0x7b14…1a66 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:51), which serves the markets of every generation, at the point of the contract flow Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:134, only when the optical flags carry BEFORE_FEE_DISTRIBUTION (4) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/libraries/BitFlag.sol:16); the optical code stays deployed unchanged and its sender checks pass (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/BaseOptical.sol:86)."
ac_5 = "The precompile calls `afterFeeDistribution(address,uint256)` (selector 0xae3bd4bd, implemented at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/BaseOptical.sol:72) on the market optical through evm.Call with caller the generation 2 FeeAccumulator address 0x7b14…1a66 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:51), at the point of the contract flow Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:161, only when the optical flags carry AFTER_FEE_DISTRIBUTION (8) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/libraries/BitFlag.sol:16); the optical code stays deployed unchanged and its sender checks pass (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/BaseOptical.sol:86)."
ac_6 = "`beforeTokenTransfer(address,address,address,uint256)` (selector 0x37be75a0, implemented at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/presets/LaunchpadOptical.sol:179) is called by the pool-token contract itself at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraERC20.sol:26-34, unchanged, when the optical flags carry BEFORE_TOKEN_TRANSFER (16); the token reads opticalAddress() from the pool surface, which the precompile answers from the keeper market record, so every pool-token transfer, the nested ones the precompile makes included, runs the hook with the token contract as caller and the optical sender checks pass (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/BaseOptical.sol:86)."

[req.2018]
title = "USDL stays the ERC20 contract and the launchpad holds it at the launchpad module EVM address"
ac_1 = "Params.QuoteDenom (modules/launchpad/types/params.go:17, value \"uusdl\" at modules/launchpad/types/params.go:31, checked by ValidateDenom at modules/launchpad/types/params.go:51) is replaced by Params.QuoteToken, the USDL contract address 0x85FcD13735F4309833A503EE804ea32395851479 (contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:14, Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:86), and the quote_denom field of api/launchpad/tx.proto becomes quote_token; MigrateV6120 writes QuoteToken over the base coin that the v6.10 handler set (node/upgrades.go:350-354), and no uusdl denom, bank metadata or pointer exists."
ac_2 = "USDL keeps its code, storage, six decimals, allowances and permit nonces; the launchpad never mints, burns or writes USDL storage, and every USDL movement is a call into the USDL contract: transferFrom(user, launchpad module EVM address, amount) with msg.sender 0x1017 against the allowance the user grants to 0x1017, and transfer(to, amount) with caller the launchpad module EVM address or a pool address, as nested calls of the precompile run (the nested-call form of precompiles/xweb/xweb.go:482) or through CallEVM in the upgrade handler (modules/evm/keeper/evm.go:81)."
ac_3 = "The keeper holds custody ledgers for the USDL at the launchpad module EVM address: HeldQuote per pool, FeeHeld for the generation 2 FeeAccumulator, and TreasuryLedger and TreasuryHeld per token for the Treasury; USDL.balanceOf(launchpad module EVM address) is at least the sum of every HeldQuote, FeeHeld and TreasuryHeld(USDL), and moves between a pool, the FeeAccumulator and the Treasury are ledger moves inside custody that emit no USDL Transfer log."
ac_4 = "Pay-first input keeps working: before swap, swapFor and syncReserves the precompile sweeps the pool address with a nested call whose caller is the pool address, USDL.transfer(launchpad module EVM address, USDL.balanceOf(pool)) when the balance is nonzero, and adds the amount to HeldQuote(pool), so USDL sent straight to the pool address before a swap counts as prepaid input as at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:175-178; the generation 2 FeeAccumulator address and the Treasury address are swept the same way before every balance read of theirs."
ac_5 = "Pool tokens stay at the pool address: sell input arrives by token.transferFrom(user, pool) or by a prior transfer to the pool, buy output leaves by token.transfer(recipient, amount) with caller the pool address (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:217), and the pool balance checks read token.balanceOf(pool) through a nested staticcall."
ac_6 = "Router and Factory pulls use allowances to 0x1017: USDL.transferFrom(caller, launchpad module EVM address, amount) for buys and creation fees (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/periphery/Router.sol:188, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/periphery/Router.sol:165, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:81) and token.transferFrom(caller, pool, amount) for sells and the first leg of a token-for-token swap (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/periphery/Router.sol:215, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/periphery/Router.sol:251); the *WithPermit variants call permit(holder, 0x1017, value, deadline, v, r, s) on the token contract through a nested call and ignore its failure as Launch-x:contracts/contracts/periphery/Router.sol:292-314 does, then pull; the intermediate USDL of a token-for-token swap (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/periphery/Router.sol:263) is a ledger move from HeldQuote of the first pool to HeldQuote of the second."
ac_7 = "Pool and FeeAccumulator USDL payouts are real USDL.transfer calls from the launchpad module EVM address to the recipient: sell output (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:239), claim, burn to `0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD`, airdrop claims, optical surplus claims and legacy airdrop claims (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:180, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:196, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:266, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:389, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:463); the buy fee is a ledger move from HeldQuote(pool) to FeeHeld (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:220-224) and sendLpRewards a ledger move from FeeHeld to HeldQuote(pool) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:282)."

[req.2019]
title = "Swaps reproduce the pool arithmetic, fee, volume and snapshot rules exactly"
ac_1 = "Swap checks in contract order: deadline (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:171), zero input (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:172), zero recipient (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:173), prepaid input (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:178), then the optical beforeSwap reduction rules (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:186-195), each reverting with the same custom error."
ac_2 = "The fee is taken on the input with mulDiv(amountIn, feeBps, 10000) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:201); a buy prices amountIn minus fee against virtual plus real USDL (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:208-213), moves the fee from HeldQuote(pool) to FeeHeld of the generation 2 FeeAccumulator and records it (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:220-224); a sell keeps fee tokens in the pool (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:241-244)."
ac_3 = "A sell whose output exceeds real USDL reverts VirtualFloorBreached() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:232); a buy whose output exceeds the token reserve reverts InsufficientLiquidity() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:211); zero output reverts InsufficientInput() and output below minAmountOut reverts SlippageExceeded() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:247-248)."
ac_4 = "USDL volume is paidInput on buys and amountOut on sells, added to cumulativeVolume and to the buy or sell cumulative field (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:250-254); the price snapshot is taken only when volume is at least 1 bps of effective USDL and 60 seconds passed since the last snapshot (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:406-415), into an eight-slot ring."
ac_5 = "After the swap the precompile emits InputAdjustment when paidInput differs from amountIn (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:257), calls afterSwap and requires its selector (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:259-263), reverts InvalidBalance() unless HeldQuote(pool) is at least realUsdlBalance and token.balanceOf(pool) is at least tokenReserve (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:268), and emits Swap at 0x1017 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:273)."
ac_6 = "The dynamic fee uses ProtocolConfig parameters with the holder concentration term fixed at 0 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:375-396) through FeeLib (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/libraries/FeeLib.sol:22), which the keeper implements in CalculateDynamicFee (modules/launchpad/types/math.go:179)."
ac_7 = "syncReserves sweeps the pool address, sets realUsdlBalance to HeldQuote(pool) and tokenReserve to token.balanceOf(pool), and emits PoolStateUpdated at 0x1017 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:279-291)."

[req.2020]
title = "Market creation deploys a pool token, a pool surface and a fee right as the Factory did"
ac_1 = "createMarket through the Router or Factory surface or 0x1017 validates name and symbol (modules/launchpad/types/market.go:36) and the virtual defaults, fee strategy and optical code as Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:115-117 does (reverting ZeroAddress()), and charges the creation fee by USDL.transferFrom(caller, launchpad module EVM address, creationFee) credited to TreasuryLedger and TreasuryHeld of the generation 2 Treasury address read from SidioraFactory slot 6 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:30) and recorded in modules/launchpad/keeper/testdata/v6120/layout.json, with Deposited(USDL, depositor, creationFee) emitted at the Treasury address (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/periphery/Router.sol:163-167, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:79-83); a failed pull reverts with the USDL revert data wrapped as TransferFromFailed() as TransferHelper does."
ac_2 = "The pool token is a real SidioraERC20 contract created by a nested CREATE2 with caller the generation 2 SidioraFactory address 0x3993…8830 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:37), salt keccak256(abi.encodePacked(creator, name, symbol, nonce)) with the per-creator nonce of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:120-121, and init code SidioraERC20(name, symbol, virtualToken, factory) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:123-125), so its deploymentFactory is 0x3993…8830 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:37) and its whole supply starts at that address with six decimals (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraERC20.sol:40-49)."
ac_3 = "The pool address is the exact address predictPoolAddress(token, creator, optical) returns (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:166-173): CREATE2 from 0x3993…8830 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:37) with salt keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token)) over the beacon proxy init code of 0x0c60…71BE (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:79) and initialize calldata built with the generation 2 role addresses (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:128-144); the precompile installs the 41-byte surface there with SetCode (modules/evm/keeper/code.go:23) and nonce 1, and when the address already holds code or a nonzero nonce the call reverts with empty revert data as Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:182 does."
ac_4 = "In the contract order of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:147-163 the precompile authorizes the pool at the generation 2 FeeAccumulator, mints the fee right in the generation 2 collection at nextTokenId (slot 11) with its strategy (slot 12) and pool (slot 13), writes the PoolRegistry metadata creator, token, optical, nftId, createdAt and createdBlock (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/interfaces/IPoolRegistry.sol:15) and the keeper market record, then runs bindPool(pool) and transfer(pool, virtualToken) on the token with caller 0x3993…8830 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:37) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:153-154), so the token transfer reads opticalAddress() from a pool that already exists (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraERC20.sol:26-34)."
ac_5 = "Market creation emits Initialized(1) at the pool address, PoolNFTMinted and Transfer at the collection, NftMint, PoolRegistered, TokenDeployed and MarketCreated of the EventEmitter family at 0x1017, and MarketCreated(address,address,address,uint256,address) at 0x3993…8830 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:37) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:159-163); the token contract emits its own ERC20 Transfer logs; no pointer is registered, so the pointer gas term of requirement 2.26 is 0 for market creation."

[req.2021]
title = "Fees split, accrue and distribute as FeeAccumulator and FeesRouter did"
ac_1 = "recordFee splits the buy fee into protocol cut protocolFeeBps/10000 and pool cut, applies the optical beforeFeeDistribution adjustment with InsufficientSurplus when it raises the pool cut (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:135), moves the protocol cut from FeeHeld to TreasuryLedger and TreasuryHeld of the Treasury with Deposited(USDL, 0x7b14…1a66, cut) emitted at the Treasury address (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:150-155), calls afterFeeDistribution and requires its selector (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:161) and emits FeeRecorded (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:164) at the generation 2 FeeAccumulator address 0x7b14…1a66 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:51)."
ac_2 = "claim pays the accumulated pool fees to the recipient by USDL.transfer from the launchpad module EVM address and reverts NoFeesAccumulated() at zero (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:169-184); burn transfers them to `0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD` (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:187-200); sendLpRewards moves them from FeeHeld to HeldQuote of the pool reserve (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:272-286)."
ac_3 = "The FeesRouter role checks the caller holds the fee right of the pool in the generation 2 collection (ownerOf) and the strategy of that fee right, and emits FeeDistributed at 0x1017 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/periphery/FeesRouter.sol:124); the keeper requireFeeRightsHolder (modules/launchpad/keeper/fees.go:12) reads the fee-right store keyed by collection and id."
ac_4 = "The FeeAccumulator keeps one totalLiabilities and requires FeeHeld to cover it plus the new amount (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:478-480); the mirror FeeFlow event is emitted at 0x1017 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:470)."

[req.2022]
title = "Airdrops snapshot holdings and pay pro rata with the contract rounding"
ac_1 = "triggerAirdrop opens epoch e+1 for the pool with the airdrop balance, the eligible supply and the snapshot block block.number-1 as Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:203-230 does, reading getPastTotalSupply and getPastBalance of the pool and dead addresses from the pool-token contract by nested staticcall; the keeper stores the epoch fields of FeeAccumulator slots 15 to 18 and no entitlement table."
ac_2 = "claimAirdrop pays holder balance at the snapshot times the epoch amount over the eligible supply by USDL.transfer from the launchpad module EVM address, refuses the pool, the `0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD` address and zero (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:250), refuses a second claim with AlreadyClaimed() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:251) and gives the rounding residue to the final claimant (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:248-269); the holder balance at the snapshot is getPastBalance(holder, snapshotBlock) read from the pool-token contract by nested staticcall."
ac_3 = "Open airdrop epochs of migrated pools keep their snapshot: MigrateV6120 carries airdropSnapshotBlock and the epoch fields (FeeAccumulator slots 15 to 18), and a claim after the upgrade reads the same token checkpoints the contract read, so it pays what the contract would have paid; modules/launchpad/keeper/history.go and its BeforeBalanceChange hook (node/app.go:808-809) stay as they are for the other launchpad flows."
ac_4 = "claimLegacyAirdrop verifies the Merkle proof over keccak256(pool, epoch, holder, amount) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:453) against legacyAirdropRoot (slot 23) and legacyAirdropRemaining (slot 24), both migrated."

[req.2023]
title = "Step 1 of MigrateV6120 moves the USDL held by launchpad contracts into custody at the launchpad module EVM address"
ac_1 = "Step 1 reads USDL.balanceOf of every pool address of generations 1 and 2, of both FeeAccumulator addresses and of both Treasury addresses (0x15405D535ce533BfFb98c83e42f4DD242AA5e079 (Launch-x:protocol/addresses.go:84) and the generation 2 Treasury address read from SidioraFactory slot 6 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:30) and recorded in modules/launchpad/keeper/testdata/v6120/layout.json) by StaticCallEVM (modules/evm/keeper/evm.go:157) and refuses with \"upgrade v6.12.0: launchpad: usdl balance differs from golden\" when a balance differs from modules/launchpad/keeper/testdata/v6120/usdl.json."
ac_2 = "For each pool and FeeAccumulator address with a nonzero balance the step calls CallEVM (modules/evm/keeper/evm.go:81) with from the holding contract and data USDL.transfer(launchpad module EVM address, balance), before any surface is installed, and credits HeldQuote(pool) or FeeHeld; the contracts have no withdraw function, which is why the transfer runs from their address (head decision 3)."
ac_3 = "For each Treasury the step calls withdraw(token, 0x1017, getBalance(token)) and then recoverSurplus(token, 0x1017, surplus) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:58-70, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:87-94) through CallEVM from the DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE holder named in the fixture, after a hasRole(0x00, holder) staticcall confirms the holding, for every token the fixture lists; the withdrawn ledger amounts are credited to TreasuryLedger of the generation 2 Treasury and the full amounts to TreasuryHeld, so nothing stays behind a retired address."
ac_4 = "USDL allowances and permit nonces are untouched because USDL storage is untouched; users who traded through the Router grant a new allowance to 0x1017, the spender of the pulls of requirement 2.18, and the migration record of contracts/launchpad.md lists this."
ac_5 = "Step 1 runs first inside MigrateV6120, needs no Minter permission and no MintCoins, and its result is checked: USDL.balanceOf(launchpad module EVM address) after the step equals its value before plus the sum moved, and the custody invariant of requirement 2.28 holds."

[req.2024]
title = "Step 2 migrates every generation 1 and generation 2 pool as a generation 2 pool"
ac_1 = "migratePools lists the pools of each generation from the PoolRegistry _allPools array (slot 6, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/PoolRegistry.sol:23) of 0x7684…BA0b and 0x1dC3…4Ba7 and refuses when a pool code hash is not the code hash of a generation pool proxy recorded in modules/launchpad/keeper/testdata/v6120/layout.json."
ac_2 = "Each pool state field is read from its slot (tokenAddress 0, usdlAddress 1, opticalAddress 2, feeAccumulator 3, eventEmitter 4, protocolConfig 5, guardian 6, virtualUsdlReserve 7, realUsdlBalance 8, tokenReserve 9, creationTimestamp 10, cumulativeVolume 11, priceSnapshots 12-19, snapshotIndex 20, snapshotCount 21, accumulatedUsdlFees 22, accumulatedTokenFees 23, factory 24, pendingGuardian 25, lastSnapshotTimestamp 26, cumulativeBuyUsdlVolume 27, cumulativeSellUsdlVolume 28) as layout.json records them for the generation implementation, into the keeper Market record."
ac_3 = "Pool tokens stay the deployed SidioraERC20 contracts with code and storage unchanged; step 2 reads token.balanceOf(pool) and totalSupply by StaticCallEVM (modules/evm/keeper/evm.go:157), checks holders.json against balanceOf with their sum equal to totalSupply, and writes nothing at the token address."
ac_4 = "For each pool the step sets RealQuote to min(realUsdlBalance, the USDL moved from the pool in step 1) and TokenReserve to min(tokenReserve, token.balanceOf(pool)), and records the book-held delta of requirement 2.38 when book and held differ, so InvalidBalance (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:268) holds for every migrated pool."
ac_5 = "Every migrated pool becomes a generation 2 pool (ruling 5): its factory, feeAccumulator, protocolConfig and eventEmitter fields are set to 0x3993…8830 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:37), 0x7b14…1a66 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:51), 0xF366…20C6 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:16) and 0x622E…3EF6 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:9), its fee right moves to the generation 2 collection, it is authorized at the generation 2 FeeAccumulator and registered at the generation 2 PoolRegistry, and the generation 1 ProtocolConfig values that differ from generation 2 are written to the migration log."
ac_6 = "Pool-token allowances, permit nonces and checkpoints stay in the token contracts, so getPastBalance, getPastTotalSupply, getPastVotes, permit, nonces, DOMAIN_SEPARATOR and PERMIT_TYPEHASH keep answering at the token addresses; Paused (the Pausable slot of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/Pausable.sol:13) and guardian state of each pool migrate into the market record."

[req.2025]
title = "Step 3 migrates fee rights, roles, FeeAccumulator accounting and optical bindings"
ac_1 = "Fee rights of the generation 2 collection keep their ids; fee rights of the generation 1 collection 0xDF73…e190 (Launch-x:protocol/addresses.go:27) are minted again in the generation 2 collection at nextTokenId in generation 1 id order, each with holder from _owners (slot 2), approval from _tokenApprovals (slot 4), operator approvals from _operatorApprovals (slot 5) for the fixture operators, strategy from _feeStrategy (slot 12) and pool from _poolAddress (slot 13), and the collection fields of slots 2-9, 11-13, 15 and 16-17 of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraNFT.sol:18-30 and Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/ERC721Base.sol:11 migrate, among them the per-holder _balances (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/ERC721Base.sol:14), the enumeration arrays _allTokens, _allTokensIndex, _ownedTokens and _ownedTokensIndex (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/ERC721Enumerable.sol:9-12) rebuilt over the merged ids, poolTokenId per pool and poolIndexMigrationCursor (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraNFT.sol:25-29), and poolIndexReady set true once every pool is indexed (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraNFT.sol:30); the fee-right receiver hook is not called on import."
ac_2 = "Role memberships other than DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE migrate from each role _roles mapping (slot 0, or slot 10 in the collection) for the accounts listed in the fixture and verified by storage read, generation 1 holders merged into the generation 2 role; DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE is not carried, so registeredDefaultAdminCount() returns 0 at every role address and administration runs through requirement 2.40."
ac_3 = "FeeAccumulator accounting of both generations merges into the generation 2 FeeAccumulator: _accumulatedFees, _protocolFeesPending, _airdropBalance, _airdropEpoch, _airdropEpochAmount, _airdropClaimed (for the fixture claimants), _lpRewardsBalance, _opticalSurplus, totalLiabilities, the airdrop snapshot fields (slots 15 to 18), accountingInitialized and the legacy airdrop fields (slots 22 to 24)."
ac_4 = "Each pool keeps its optical address; optical contracts stay deployed and unchanged and are called by the precompile with the callers they accept (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/BaseOptical.sol:86), the PoolRegistry metadata (slot 4) of every pool migrates with nftId (the new id for a generation 1 fee right), createdAt and createdBlock, and OPTICAL_GRANTER_ROLE of LaunchpadOpticalFactory (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/LaunchpadOpticalFactory.sol:106) migrates to the generation 2 FeeAccumulator role table."
ac_5 = "MigrateV6120 returns its first error wrapped as \"upgrade v6.12.0: launchpad: <error>\" by the caller in the upgrade handler; it writes nothing outside the launchpad and EVM stores, USDL balances change only through the nested ERC20 calls of step 1, and the whole migration is one cached context committed only on success."
ac_6 = "The map from each generation 1 fee-right id to its generation 2 id is written to the migration log and stored in the keeper, served by a keeper query, and exported and imported by genesis."

[req.2026]
title = "Gas follows the existing schedule without the pointer term, extended to every served method"
ac_1 = "RequiredGas is Gas(inputBytes, writes) with BaseGas 3000, GasPerByte 16 and GasPerWrite 5000 (precompiles/launchpad/launchpad.go:15-17, precompiles/launchpad/launchpad.go:224); GasPerPointer and the pointer argument (precompiles/launchpad/launchpad.go:18) go because no pointer is registered, and the Writes table (precompiles/launchpad/launchpad.go:196) lists every state-changing method of the eleven role files."
ac_2 = "Nested evm.Call and CREATE2 gas for token deployment, USDL and pool-token transfers, optical hooks and the fee-right receiver hook is metered by the EVM, as the xweb precompile meters its callback (precompiles/xweb/xweb.go:482)."
ac_3 = "The current pinned gas test (precompiles/launchpad/launchpad_test.go:177) moves to the legacy version with its precompile and keeps its values there."

[req.2027]
title = "The new precompile is served from the v6.12.0 height and the previous one is kept below it"
ac_1 = "GetVersioned (precompiles/launchpad/setup.go:10-14) returns the new precompile under the key \"v6.12.0\" and the current one under \"v6.10\" from precompiles/launchpad/legacy/v610, which task 2.0.7 copies at 211acbc6c before any change, following the pattern of precompiles/p256/setup.go:15-24; precompiles/launchpad/versions gains v6.12.0 after v6.5 (precompiles/launchpad/versions:1) and the registration of precompiles/setup.go:183 is unchanged."
ac_2 = "0x1017 stays behind activationPrecompileGate (node/upgrades.go:498); the v6.12.0 handler switches the versioned set live explicitly and a node restarted after the upgrade restores it from state, as xweb is switched (node/upgrades.go:216-236, node/upgrades.go:276-282); no node/tags entry is added and the handler never reads GetDoneHeight; the plan names v6.9 (node/upgrades.go:93) and v6.10 (node/upgrades.go:102) stay as they are."
ac_3 = "The v6.12.0 handler (baseline task 1.0.3) runs RunMigrations, moveSidioraMintAuthority and migrateSIDHolders, then its hook table in the order the createV6120Pointers hook of baseline task 1.2.4, launchpad MigrateV6120, pricefeed InitV6120, perps SeedV6120 and spot InitV6120, so MigrateV6120 is the first domain hook, wrapping each error as \"upgrade v6.12.0: <hook>: <error>\"; this domain supplies MigrateV6120, its EVMReader interface and the legacy keeper accessor that task 1.3.100 wires in node/app.go."

[req.2028]
title = "Invariants bind the USDL held at the launchpad module EVM address and the pool-token balances to the contract accounting"
ac_1 = "SolvencyInvariant (modules/launchpad/keeper/invariants.go:20) checks, for every market, that HeldQuote(pool) is at least realUsdlBalance and token.balanceOf(pool) is at least tokenReserve, the condition of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:268."
ac_2 = "LiabilitiesInvariant checks that FeeHeld is at least totalLiabilities (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:478-480) and that TreasuryHeld is at least TreasuryLedger for every token, and is registered in RegisterInvariants (modules/launchpad/keeper/invariants.go:13)."
ac_3 = "CustodyInvariant checks that USDL.balanceOf(launchpad module EVM address), read by StaticCallEVM, is at least the sum of every HeldQuote, FeeHeld and TreasuryHeld(USDL), and that the custody ledgers change only by sweeps, pulls, payouts and the ledger moves of requirement 2.18."

[req.2029]
title = "Module parameters equal the ProtocolConfig values of the active generation"
ac_1 = "DefaultParams (modules/launchpad/types/params.go:34) sets ConcentrationWeight 0 and CreationFee 1000000, the ProtocolConfig values (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/ProtocolConfig.sol:45-54); today it holds 100 and 100000000, a required change."
ac_2 = "MigrateV6120 writes one parameter set read from the generation 2 ProtocolConfig storage (slots 2 to 11) and refuses when it fails Validate (modules/launchpad/types/params.go:50); the generation 1 ProtocolConfig values that differ are written to the migration log and not applied (ruling 5)."
ac_3 = "Validate adds the ProtocolConfig bounds: concentrationWeight must be 0 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/ProtocolConfig.sol:84), decay and volatility weights at most 10000 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/ProtocolConfig.sol:79-90), virtual defaults fit uint112 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/ProtocolConfig.sol:100), protocolFeeBps at most 5000 (modules/launchpad/types/params.go:11) and baseFeeBps within min and max (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/ProtocolConfig.sol:60)."
ac_4 = "Parameters change only through MsgUpdateParams from the governance authority (modules/launchpad/keeper/msg_server.go:14), which emits ConfigUpdated at 0x1017 for each changed key."

[req.2030]
title = "The intents crate decodes the launchpad events of the new interface"
ac_1 = "The launchpad decode of the intents crate (human/crates/layerx-intents/src/precompile.rs:557) decodes the twelve EventEmitter launchpad events emitted at LAUNCHPAD_PRECOMPILE (human/crates/layerx-intents/src/precompile.rs:24), which replace the logs the generation 2 EventEmitter emitted for launchpad flows, and PrecompileEventKind (human/crates/layerx-intents/src/precompile.rs:28) lists them with their topic0."
ac_2 = "The intent map (human/crates/layerx-intents/src/precompile.rs:1005-1014) maps Swap to LaunchpadSwap, MarketCreated to LaunchpadCreate, FeeStrategyChanged to LaunchpadFeeStrategy and FeeDistributed by strategy to LaunchpadFeesClaim, LaunchpadFeesBurn, LaunchpadAirdropExecute and LaunchpadLpRewards, with the vocabulary variants of human/crates/layerx-intents/src/vocabulary.rs:134-145."
ac_3 = "every_abi_event_is_declared_with_its_computed_topic (human/crates/layerx-intents/tests/precompile_router.rs:203) keeps passing with LAUNCHPAD_ABI (human/crates/layerx-intents/tests/precompile_router.rs:26) now the new abi.json."

[req.2031]
title = "The hosted indexer and gateway read the new launchpad interface"
ac_1 = "The hosted indexer registry entry (\"launchpad\", 0x1017) (platform/hosted/indexer/src/abi.rs:41) loads the new abi.json, and signatures_and_topics_match_solidity (platform/hosted/indexer/src/abi.rs:637) covers the twelve launchpad events."
ac_2 = "The gateway launchpad probe changes from getMarketCount() (platform/hosted/gateway/src/capabilities.rs:40) to getPoolCount() of the new interface, selector 0x8eec5d70, sent to LAUNCHPAD_PRECOMPILE (platform/hosted/gateway/src/evm.rs:47), and its answer still decodes as one word (platform/hosted/gateway/src/capabilities.rs:87)."
ac_3 = "The indexer ingest test replays a Swap and a MarketCreated log at 0x1017 and stores one row each."

[req.2032]
title = "The launchpad backend binds the precompile through its manifest roles"
ac_1 = "The deployment manifest accepts role kind \"surface\" for the mandatory roles and adds role LaunchpadPrecompile at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001017 with kind \"precompile\": Validate (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/manifest.go:113) accepts both kinds, exempts them from the runtime hash check and requires the implementation fields to be empty as for \"direct\" (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/manifest.go:177)."
ac_2 = "current.json keeps one generation: every role keeps its generation 2 address with kind \"surface\" (the SidioraPool family served by the pool surfaces, SidioraNFT at the generation 2 collection), USDL stays at 0x85FcD13735F4309833A503EE804ea32395851479 kind \"direct\" (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:86), LaunchpadPrecompile is added, deploymentVersion and activationHeight (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:3-6) take the v6.12.0 values, settlement USDL six decimals stays, and the governance block (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:101-107) stays."
ac_3 = "The decode registry (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/registry.go:158) binds LaunchpadPrecompile at 0x1017 to the EventEmitter ABI and dispatches each log there by topic0 to its event, beside the generation 2 EventEmitter binding that keeps decoding the logs of other systems (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/registry.go:234)."
ac_4 = "parseContractAddresses (Launch-x:shared/chain/contracts.go:67) accepts kind \"surface\" and the LaunchpadPrecompile role, and CreateContracts (Launch-x:shared/chain/contracts.go:93) binds each role at its generation 2 address with its role ABI and binds the EventEmitter ABI at 0x1017 for the launchpad family events."
ac_5 = "protocol/addresses.go keeps the generation 1 addresses (Launch-x:protocol/addresses.go:20-29) for historical decoding, marks them retired from the v6.12.0 height, and adds the precompile address 0x1017 and the generation 2 role addresses as the active set."

[req.2033]
title = "The domain completes with the launchpad package set passing"
ac_1 = "Task 2.3.99 runs go test ./modules/launchpad/... ./precompiles/launchpad/... once after every other task of the domain is done."
ac_2 = "TestLaunchpadDomainWiring builds the keeper and the precompile together and runs createMarket, buy, sell, claimFees and a migrated pool read in one store."

[req.2034]
title = "Re-entrancy locks and nested calls follow the contract guards"
ac_1 = "swap, swapFor and syncReserves of a pool run under a per-pool lock held in the transient store of the precompile run; a second state-changing entry for the same pool while the lock is held, from an optical hook, a token hook or any nested call, reverts ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall() (0x3ee5aeb5) as the nonReentrant guard of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:152, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:159 and Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraPool.sol:279 does (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/ReentrancyGuard.sol:15)."
ac_2 = "The FeeAccumulator role holds one lock across recordFee, claim, burn, triggerAirdrop, claimAirdrop, claimAirdropEpoch, sendLpRewards, claimOpticalSurplus, claimLegacyAirdrop and allocateLegacyAirdrop as its nonReentrant functions do (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:112, :172, :189, :205, :236, :242, :274, :364, :380, :449), the Treasury role holds the lock of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:23-31 and reverts ReentrantCall() (0x37ed32e8), and the Router and FeesRouter roles hold the locks of their nonReentrant entry points."
ac_3 = "Locks live only for one precompile run and are released on return and on revert; view functions are answered while a lock is held, so the opticalAddress() read of a pool-token transfer and the getReserves() read of an optical hook succeed during a swap."
ac_4 = "Before each nested call (optical hook, USDL or pool-token transfer, permit, fee-right receiver hook) the precompile writes every keeper change of the run so far, so the nested call and any view it makes see the committed outer state, in the order of the contract flow: reserves and snapshot before afterSwap, fee split before afterFeeDistribution."
ac_5 = "A nested call that reverts reverts the whole precompile call with the nested revert data, except the permit of the *WithPermit variants, whose failure the contract ignores (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/periphery/Router.sol:292-314); the fee-right receiver hook follows the contract rule: a wrong return value or an empty revert gives NonERC721Receiver() (0x80526d0c) and any other revert data is returned unchanged (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraNFT.sol:71-77, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/ERC721Base.sol:81-92)."

[req.2035]
title = "The Treasury role is served at the generation 2 Treasury address over a keeper ledger"
ac_1 = "The generation 2 Treasury address read from SidioraFactory slot 6 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraFactory.sol:30) and recorded in modules/launchpad/keeper/testdata/v6120/layout.json holds the surface runtime and serves the Treasury ABI of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:13 (17 functions, 8 events, 19 errors, the eleventh role file of requirement 2.1) for the treasury of every generation, the generation 1 Treasury 0x15405D535ce533BfFb98c83e42f4DD242AA5e079 (Launch-x:protocol/addresses.go:84) being retired by requirement 2.36."
ac_2 = "deposit(token, amount) (0x47e7ef24) pulls token.transferFrom(caller, launchpad module EVM address, amount) for a DEPOSITOR_ROLE caller, credits the received amount measured by balanceOf before and after to TreasuryLedger and TreasuryHeld and emits Deposited(token, caller, received) at the Treasury address (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:46-54, ITreasury.sol:14); recordDeposit(token, amount) (0x1e578bae) sweeps the Treasury address, requires amount at most TreasuryHeld minus TreasuryLedger and credits the ledger (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:79-85)."
ac_3 = "getBalance(token) (0xf8b2cb4f) returns TreasuryLedger(token) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:73-75) and rises after every createMarket by the creation fee and after every recordFee by the protocol cut; eventEmitter() (0x9ff78c30) returns 0x622E…3EF6 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:9); DEPOSITOR_ROLE(), hasRole and getRoleAdmin answer from the migrated role table; a token address without code, or whose balanceOf staticcall fails or returns other than 32 bytes, reverts InvalidToken() (0xc1ab6dc1) as _actualBalance does (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:96-101)."
ac_4 = "withdraw (0xd9caed12, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:58-70) and recoverSurplus (0x72df7f5b, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:87-94) revert `AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(address,bytes32)` (0xe2517d3f) with the caller and 0x00 at the surface (ruling 7) and run only through MsgTreasuryWithdraw of requirement 2.40; initialize (0x485cc955, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:38-42) reverts AlreadyInitialized() and upgradeToAndCall reverts as in requirement 2.13."
ac_5 = "MigrateV6120 carries the Treasury _balances ledger (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:16) of both generations per token listed in the fixture into TreasuryLedger, and the DEPOSITOR_ROLE members of both generations into the role table of the generation 2 Treasury."

[req.2036]
title = "Generation 1 role addresses are retired and point at their generation 2 replacement"
ac_1 = "MigrateV6120 installs at the generation 1 SidioraFactory, Router, Quoter, ProtocolConfig, FeeAccumulator, PoolRegistry, fee-right collection and FeesRouter addresses (Launch-x:protocol/addresses.go:20-29), the generation 1 Treasury 0x15405D535ce533BfFb98c83e42f4DD242AA5e079 (Launch-x:protocol/addresses.go:84) and the generation 1 OpticalRegistry (Launch-x:protocol/addresses.go:95) the fixed retirement runtime that reverts Retired(address) (0xda9d2e31) carrying the generation 2 address of the same role, for every selector, after their USDL is moved in step 1."
ac_2 = "Storage at the retired addresses is left as it was at the halt height, the generation 1 EventEmitter (Launch-x:protocol/addresses.go:20) and PoolBeacon (Launch-x:protocol/addresses.go:29) keep their code, the Timelock and GovernanceModule (Launch-x:protocol/addresses.go:85-86) keep their code, and generation 1 pool addresses are not retired: they serve as generation 2 pools by requirement 2.24."
ac_3 = "The retired list (address, role, replacement) is written to the migration log, served by a keeper query and listed in contracts/launchpad.md section 21, and the release runbook announces it before the halt."

[req.2037]
title = "Contracts that stay deployed keep working against the surfaces"
ac_1 = "The generation 2 EventEmitter 0x622E…3EF6 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:9) stays deployed and keeps serving the other systems; its authorization reads (_isAuthorized, _requireTyped and _requirePool at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/EventEmitter.sol:165-190 and Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/EventEmitter.sol:216-227) go to the PoolRegistry, FeeAccumulator and Factory surfaces, which answer from the keeper, and the launchpad family events are emitted at 0x1017 by requirement 2.16, so MirrorFailed (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/FeeAccumulator.sol:471, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/data/PoolRegistry.sol:69, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/periphery/FeesRouter.sol:19) is never emitted after the upgrade."
ac_2 = "The generation 2 OpticalRegistry 0x0FB5…fcF0 (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:72), LaunchpadOpticalFactory and every optical keep their code; createLaunchpadOptical (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/LaunchpadOpticalFactory.sol:79) calls authorizeOptical (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/LaunchpadOpticalFactory.sol:106) at the generation 2 FeeAccumulator surface, which accepts it through the migrated OPTICAL_GRANTER_ROLE, and onlyAttachedPool (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/BaseOptical.sol:86) passes because isRegisteredPool at the generation 2 PoolRegistry surface answers for pools of every generation."
ac_3 = "The generation 2 PoolBeacon 0x0c60…71BE (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:79) keeps its code and is the beacon named in the predicted pool address of requirement 2.20; BeaconCallFailed and the beacon functions answer as the contract does."
ac_4 = "Operations queued in the Timelock or GovernanceModule that call a DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE method at a surface revert `AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(address,bytes32)` (0xe2517d3f) when executed; EmergencyPauseController.pauseTargets (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/EmergencyPauseController.sol:44, :87-95) calling pause() at a pool surface reverts Unauthorized() unless the controller is the pool guardian, exactly as at the halt height, within the 150000 and 30000 gas budgets of the controller."
ac_5 = "The meta-ag SidioraAdapter reads the Router, Quoter and PoolRegistry addresses it holds (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/adapters/SidioraAdapter.sol:92), which are generation 2 surfaces, and approves its Router (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/adapters/SidioraAdapter.sol:257-258); since pulls run with spender 0x1017, the release runbook calls setSidioraRouter(0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001017) through its admin, and getPoolByToken answers for tokens of every generation."

[req.2038]
title = "Book and held amounts are reconciled per pool and the delta is recorded"
ac_1 = "For every migrated pool MigrateV6120 compares the book (realUsdlBalance, tokenReserve) with the held amounts (USDL moved from the pool in step 1, token.balanceOf(pool)), uses the smaller value of each pair, and stores the book-held delta (pool, asset, book, held, delta) in a keeper record, writes it to the migration log and serves it by a keeper query; nothing is minted or topped up."
ac_2 = "modules/launchpad/keeper/testdata/v6120/pools.json lists the known deltas at the survey height: USDL 0x90665CF0… minus 100, 0x67e1b3d8… minus 50 and 0x26Fd86Ef… minus 1,508.850948, and pool tokens 0x67e1b3d8… minus 130,368,747,608 and 0x7bF2f964… minus 5e12 (base units), and the step refuses when a pool not listed at the halt height shows a delta larger than the fixture tolerance."
ac_3 = "The golden fixture includes generation 1 pool 0xEeA16aC55AaE47c484EBef02eb1186aD606e1BF9 and generation 2 pool 0xCE20Da50F92D21d8BeE497910c782E9Aa25b6263 with their reads at H, and the golden pool count is the 45 generation 1 and 4 generation 2 pools of the registries."

[req.2039]
title = "MigrateV6120 guards the keeper state, migrates pause state and keeps the legacy replay"
ac_1 = "MigrateV6120 refuses with \"upgrade v6.12.0: launchpad: native markets exist\" when GetMarketCount (modules/launchpad/keeper/keeper.go:99-102) is above 0 at the halt height, so no native market created before the upgrade collides with the imported indexes."
ac_2 = "The pause flag of every pool (the Pausable slot at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/base/Pausable.sol:13) and the guardian and pending guardian migrate into the market record, so paused() and emergencyPaused() return the halt-height values and a paused pool refuses swaps after the upgrade."
ac_3 = "The v6.10 keeper and types are copied by task 2.0.7 at 211acbc6c into modules/launchpad/legacy/v610/keeper and modules/launchpad/legacy/v610/types (packages keeperv610 and typesv610) over the same store key, the legacy precompile of requirement 2.27 is built on them, and a legacy accessor beside LaunchpadK() (precompiles/utils/expected_keepers.go:54) exposes them, so blocks below the v6.12.0 height replay with the code that produced them."

[req.2040]
title = "Administration runs through governance messages"
ac_1 = "MsgUpdateParams (modules/launchpad/keeper/msg_server.go:14) is the only path for role administration: its role_grants and role_revokes fields grant and revoke non-admin roles in the migrated role table under the governance authority and emit RoleGranted and RoleRevoked at the surface of the role, and every DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE method at a surface reverts `AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(address,bytes32)` (0xe2517d3f), the single accepted divergence (ruling 7)."
ac_2 = "MsgTreasuryWithdraw (authority, token, to, amount, surplus flag), declared in api/launchpad/tx.proto and registered in modules/launchpad/types/codec.go beside MsgUpdateParams (modules/launchpad/types/codec.go:16, modules/launchpad/types/codec.go:19), runs only under the governance authority, pays out from TreasuryHeld by token.transfer from the launchpad module EVM address, debits TreasuryLedger for a withdraw and only the surplus for a recovery, and emits Withdrawn (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/interfaces/ITreasury.sol:15) or SurplusRecovered (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/protocol/Treasury.sol:22) at the Treasury address."

