# Feature 4: the spot venue as the PECOR precompile set (contracts/spot.md).

[feature.4]
name = "spot"
scope = "The spot venue of Paxeer X Network as the PECOR precompile set at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 to 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001025 backed by the new modules/spot keeper, pricing every trade from the pricefeed index price, holding USDL and every bridged ERC20 as ERC20 balances of the spot module EVM address and uhpx and the SID denom as bank balances of the spot module account, executing resting limit and stop orders in bounded EndBlock steps, and serving the application ABI selectors with the added error entries of contracts/spot.md#added-error-entries; the application changes its addresses and the items of contracts/spot.md#hyperpax-call-sequence (feature 6), and the node wiring is the baseline wiring task 1.3.100."
requirements = ["4001", "4002", "4003", "4004", "4005", "4006", "4007", "4008", "4009", "4010", "4011", "4012", "4013", "4014", "4015", "4016", "4017", "4018", "4019", "4020", "4021", "4022", "4023", "4024", "4025", "4026", "4027"]
completion_task = "4.3.99"

[req.4001]
title = "The spot precompile set serves the PECOR interface at fixed addresses with the application selectors"
ac_1 = "0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 serves PECOR, 0x1022 PECOROrders, 0x1023 PECORStopOrders, 0x1024 PECORQuoter and 0x1025 PECORVault, the five contracts the Hyperpax application resolves (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/addresses.ts:31-51), built by precompiles/spot NewPrecompileSet, which returns the address map and an error, and registered in node/app.go after GetCustomPrecompiles by the baseline wiring task 1.3.100, which returns the constructor error."
ac_2 = "Every function selector, event topic and error selector of the six served ABIs equals the value computed from the application ABI files (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:313 for marketBuy) extended by the entries of contracts/spot.md#added-error-entries, and the golden fixtures under precompiles/spot/testdata record each one."
ac_3 = "Each method keeps the state mutability of the application ABI except multicall: view methods are callable through eth_call, swapExactInNative and depositNative are payable, every other write refuses a non-zero value with ValidateNonPayable (precompiles/common/precompiles.go:374), and multicall is served nonpayable as the source declares it (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:589-605), where the application ABI marks it view (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:404), an entry feature 6 changes."
ac_4 = "0x1026 and 0x1027 carry no code: vault share tokens are ERC20 pointers returned by `shareTokens(address)` and the record maps no router behaviour; a call to either address behaves as a call to an account with no code."
ac_5 = "Every spot call of the Hyperpax application keeps its method and argument list (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:164-167, Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:297-300, Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:425-428, Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotQuoter.ts:139-142); the application changes only the items of contracts/spot.md#hyperpax-call-sequence, made by feature 6: the five addresses, the removal of the PriceOracle address, the PAX and SID token constants at 6 decimals, the removal of WPAX9 and the wrap path, the stable list reduced to USDL, the added error entries and the multicall mutability."
ac_6 = "A call before the v6.12.0 upgrade height is not served: the baseline wiring task 1.3.100 keys 0x1021 to 0x1027 to v6.12.0 in the versioned precompile maps and switches them live through the v6120Live flag the upgrade handler sets, so history below the upgrade height replays without them."

[req.4002]
title = "Tokens are ERC20 or native balances held by the spot module and settle atomically"
ac_1 = "Every spot token has a custody kind in TokenParams.kind: USDL and every bridged ERC20 are kind ERC20, held as ERC20 balances of the spot module EVM address (GetEVMAddressOrDefault, modules/evm/keeper/address.go:41), USDL being the existing contract 0x85FcD13735F4309833A503EE804ea32395851479 (contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:14) with 6 decimals (contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:16); uhpx (modules/evm/keeper/params.go:22) and the SID denom layerxbridgetypes.SidioraDenom() (modules/layerxbridge/types/keys.go:53-59) are kind NATIVE, held as bank balances of the spot module account; USDL has no bank denom and no pointer, and the book reserves of a token never exceed its custody."
ac_2 = "An ERC20 input is pulled by the rail that takes it (0x1021 for swaps and market orders, 0x1022 for limit placement, 0x1023 for stop placement, 0x1025 for deposits) through a nested evm.Call with the rail as msg.sender to transferFrom(caller, module EVM address, amount), the pattern of precompiles/xweb/xweb.go:482, so the allowance of the user is to that rail; the credited amount is the balanceOf delta of the module EVM address across the call (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/vault/PECORVault.sol:446-459). A NATIVE input moves by bank SendCoins (precompiles/utils/expected_keepers.go:100) from the caller to the spot module account with no allowance."
ac_3 = "An ERC20 payout is a transfer from the module EVM address, by a nested evm.Call inside a transaction and by CallEVM (modules/evm/keeper/evm.go:81) outside one; a NATIVE payout is a bank SendCoins from the spot module account. The module and recipient balance deltas must both equal the amount, and a token argument with no registered kind or a CW20 pointer reverts UnsupportedTransfer() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/vault/PECORVault.sol:554-565)."
ac_4 = "An ERC20 call that reverts or returns false, or a bank move that fails, reverts the whole spot call with SafeERC20FailedOperation(token) carrying the token address or the native pointer address; pull, payout, fee accrual and book update land together or not at all, through one cached context written only on success."
ac_5 = "EndBlock settles through the same keeper path as a transaction, its ERC20 legs through CallEVM, under the spot synthetic receipt of baseline task 1.0.6 (SyntheticReceiptContext(ctx, SyntheticReceiptSpot)); custody reads of an ERC20 token are balanceOf of the module EVM address through StaticCallEVM (modules/evm/keeper/evm.go:157) outside a transaction and a nested static call inside one."
ac_6 = "The PAX token is the native pointer of uhpx, so native PAX and the PAX token are one bank balance and no wrap exists: swapExactInNative and depositNative take the attached value, which the EVM has credited to the rail address, and move it as uhpx at value / 1e12 into the spot module account; a value that is not a whole multiple of 1e12 wei reverts UnsupportedInputTransfer(), the exact-input rule of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:429; swapExactInToNative and withdrawNative pay uhpx by bank send."
ac_7 = "The error `SafeERC20FailedOperation(address token)` (selector 0x5274afe7, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:1150) is returned as ABI custom error data when: An ERC20 transferFrom or transfer made by the venue that reverts or returns false, argument the token contract; a bank move made by the venue that fails, as an insufficient balance, argument the native pointer."
ac_8 = "The error `ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall()` (selector 0x3ee5aeb5, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:1145) is returned as ABI custom error data when: A call into any spot address made from inside a token call that a spot method started (a token hook calling back)."
ac_9 = "The error `UnsupportedTransfer()` (selector 0xce2d28e1, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/vault/PECORVault.sol:58) is returned as ABI custom error data when: A token argument with no registered kind or a CW20 pointer, an ERC20 move whose module or recipient balance delta differs from the amount, and a payout to the module EVM address itself (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/vault/PECORVault.sol:554-565)."
ac_10 = "The spot module account is in allowedReceivingModAcc (baseline task 1.3.100), so bank sends to it are accepted; native payouts use bank SendCoins from the module address, not SendCoinsFromModuleToAccount."

[req.4003]
title = "Prices come from the pricefeed module and the pool prices every trade by its index price"
ac_1 = "Every spot price is read through modules/pricefeed/keeper GetPrice(ctx, marketId) returning index, mark, timestamp and fresh; the spot venue uses the index price at 18 decimals and no other source, replacing the relayer oracle of the engine (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/oracle/PriceOracle.sol:183-206)."
ac_2 = "The pricefeed market id of a token comes from the tokens parameter: PAX reads market 11 (PAX) and SID reads market 12 (SID), the ids of contracts/perps-markets.md; USDL is the only stable token and prices at exactly 1e18 without a read."
ac_3 = "A token whose GetPrice reports fresh false refuses every trade and fill with StalePrice() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/oracle/PriceOracle.sol:161), and the quoter reports the stale flag instead of reverting."
ac_4 = "The gross output of a swap is amountIn x priceIn x 10^decOut / (priceOut x 10^decIn), rounded down, as PECORMath convert (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECORMath.sol:12), and the USD volume is amountIn x priceIn / 10^decIn."
ac_5 = "A non-stable token without a pricefeed market id in the tokens parameter refuses orders with InvalidOracle() and swaps with StalePrice()."
ac_6 = "PECOR `PRECISION() returns (uint256)` (0xaaf5eb68, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:77): Returns 1e18, the scale of every USD price (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:60)."
ac_7 = "PECOR `priceOracle() returns (address)` (0x2630c12f, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:469): Returns 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001020, the pricefeed precompile; every spot price is read from modules/pricefeed GetPrice (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:96)."
ac_8 = "PECOR `WETH() returns (address)` (0xad5c4648, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:116): Returns the ERC20 native pointer of uhpx registered by InitV6120, the PAX token of the venue; the engine kept a wrapped token here (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:101), which the bank model replaces."
ac_9 = "The error `StalePrice()` (selector 0x19abf40e, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/oracle/PriceOracle.sol:61) is returned as ABI custom error data when: A trade, fill or getTWAP while GetPrice reports the token price not fresh (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/oracle/PriceOracle.sol:161)."
ac_10 = "The error `InvalidOracle()` (selector 0x9589a27d, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:959) is returned as ABI custom error data when: A placement or execution on a non-stable token without a pricefeed market id in the tokens parameter."

[req.4004]
title = "Fees stack by volume tier, impact is capped, and both are recorded per trade"
ac_1 = "The fee in bps of a swap is swapFeeBps, plus tier1FeeBps when the USD volume is at least 10,000e18, plus tier2FeeBps when it is at least 100,000e18 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:743-747); the fee amount is gross x feeBps / 10000 rounded down; values come from contracts/perps-parameters.md#spot-fees."
ac_2 = "With priceImpactEnabled the impact in bps is volumeUSD x priceImpactScalarBps / reserveUSD of the output token, where reserveUSD is the spendable book of the output token at its index price, capped at MAX_IMPACT_BPS 500 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:68, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:711), and the net output is afterFee - afterFee x impact / 10000."
ac_3 = "The fee and the impact deduction stay in custody as an accrual of the output token, reserved so that no liquidity provider can withdraw them, and grow accumulatedFees of the rail that traded (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:704-720); fees and impact belong to feeCollector, not to the liquidity providers."
ac_4 = "Resting fills on 0x1022 and 0x1023 price with the order pricing set orderFeeBps, orderTier1FeeBps, orderTier2FeeBps, orderPriceImpactEnabled and orderPriceImpactScalarBps, as the order engine keeps its own set (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:114-118) with the swap-rail defaults (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:460), and accrue to the order-rail accrual shared by both addresses."
ac_5 = "Exact-output pricing searches the fee tier band whose inverse covers the target, then adds one unit until the forward net output reaches it (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:648-686)."
ac_6 = "PECOR `MAX_FEE_BPS() returns (uint256)` (0xd55be8c6, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:51): Returns 200, the cap on swapFeeBps + tier1FeeBps + tier2FeeBps (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:65, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:187-205)."
ac_7 = "PECOR `MAX_IMPACT_BPS() returns (uint256)` (0x5f3a4413, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:64): Returns 500, the cap on the impact deduction in bps (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:68)."
ac_8 = "PECOR `TIER1_THRESHOLD() returns (uint256)` (0x642ce355, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:90): Returns 10000e18; a trade of at least this USD volume adds tier1FeeBps (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:71, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:743-747)."
ac_9 = "PECOR `TIER2_THRESHOLD() returns (uint256)` (0x086d2c87, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:103): Returns 100000e18; a trade of at least this USD volume adds tier2FeeBps on top of tier1FeeBps (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:72, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:743-747)."
ac_10 = "PECOR `swapFeeBps() returns (uint256)` (0x2ffdaf89, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:741): Returns swapFeeBps, the taker fee of the swap rail (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:104)."
ac_11 = "PECOR `tier1FeeBps() returns (uint256)` (0x52999593, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:754): Returns tier1FeeBps (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:106)."
ac_12 = "PECOR `tier2FeeBps() returns (uint256)` (0xa9fbe778, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:767): Returns tier2FeeBps (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:108)."
ac_13 = "PECOR `impactScalarBps() returns (uint256)` (0xaa4186f5, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:300): Returns the priceImpactScalarBps parameter (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:113)."
ac_14 = "PECOR `priceImpactEnabled() returns (bool)` (0x384d3fe5, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:456): Returns the priceImpactEnabled parameter (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:111)."
ac_15 = "PECOR `BPS_DENOMINATOR() returns (uint256)` (0xe1a45218, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:38): Returns 10000 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:61)."
ac_16 = "The event `TieredFeeApplied(address indexed user, address indexed tokenOut, uint256 volumeUSD, uint256 feeBps, uint256 feeAmount)` (topic0 0x2e5d94e9d6c18964a316947fbe6368a89eae77275308006b99685ed7624d33b3, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:1038) is written at 0x1021 by: Every exact-input trade at 0x1021 (swapExactIn, marketBuy, marketSell, swapExactInNative, swapExactInToNative) with a non-zero fee (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:706); swapExactOut and the order fills emit none (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:291-322, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:446-458)."
ac_17 = "The event `PriceImpactApplied(address indexed user, address indexed tokenOut, uint256 impactBps, uint256 deductedAmount)` (topic0 0x2c967c87f38e293c4c2df8277028656cf8d42c2f6b5c06cd97b53eaebc8f7466, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:964) is written at 0x1021 by: Every exact-input trade at 0x1021 (swapExactIn, marketBuy, marketSell, swapExactInNative, swapExactInToNative) whose impact deduction is non-zero (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:716); swapExactOut and the order fills emit none (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:291-322, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:446-458)."

[req.4005]
title = "Market orders buy and sell against the pool with slippage and deadline"
ac_1 = "marketBuy requires a registered stablecoin and a registered non-stable token (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:625-626 rule), pulls the stablecoin, pays the token and emits MarketOrderExecuted with isBuy true (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:325-363)."
ac_2 = "A deadline that is non-zero and before the block time reverts Expired() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:132-135), and a net output below the minimum reverts InsufficientOutput() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:281)."
ac_3 = "A trade whose gross output exceeds the spendable book of the output token, or its utilization cap, reverts InsufficientLiquidity(): the source reserves the retained fee and impact (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:719-720) before it checks the net output (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:281-282, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:355-356), so the rule is gross at most spendable, which the order engine checks directly (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:450)."
ac_4 = "PECOR `marketBuy(address stablecoin, address token, uint256 stablecoinAmount, uint256 minTokenAmount, uint256 deadline) returns (uint256 tokenAmount)` (0x77a61952, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:313): Pulls stablecoinAmount of a registered stablecoin from the caller (ERC20 by transferFrom against an allowance to this rail, native by bank send), pays the net token output (gross at most the spendable book and its utilization cap), emits MarketOrderExecuted with isBuy true (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:325-363)."
ac_5 = "PECOR `marketSell(address token, address stablecoin, uint256 tokenAmount, uint256 minStablecoinAmount, uint256 deadline) returns (uint256 stablecoinAmount)` (0x57f24201, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:352): Pulls tokenAmount of a registered non-stable token (ERC20 by transferFrom against an allowance to this rail, native by bank send), pays the net stablecoin output, emits MarketOrderExecuted with isBuy false (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:366-404)."
ac_6 = "The event `MarketOrderExecuted(address indexed user, address indexed stablecoin, address indexed token, uint256 stablecoinAmount, uint256 tokenAmount, bool isBuy)` (topic0 0x0812c3288c5d540088b34db30524fa26b13055f197af021d88b59427a0dbdbbe, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:852) is written at 0x1021 by: marketBuy (isBuy true) and marketSell (isBuy false) at 0x1021 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:360, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:401)."
ac_7 = "The error `NotAStablecoin()` (selector 0x777a9be8, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:984) is returned as ABI custom error data when: The stablecoin argument is not a registered stablecoin (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:625)."
ac_8 = "The error `TokenIsStablecoin()` (selector 0xc1343a37, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:1056) is returned as ABI custom error data when: The token argument is a registered stablecoin (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:626)."
ac_9 = "The error `ZeroAmount()` (selector 0x1f2a2005, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:1066) is returned as ABI custom error data when: A zero amount on a swap, market order, placement, deposit or withdraw (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:264)."
ac_10 = "The error `Expired()` (selector 0x203d82d8, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:77) is returned as ABI custom error data when: A non-zero deadline before the block time on a swap or market order (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:132-135)."
ac_11 = "The error `InsufficientOutput()` (selector 0xbb2875c3, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:78) is returned as ABI custom error data when: A net output below the caller minimum, or a fill whose net output is zero or below the order minimum (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:281, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:449)."
ac_12 = "The error `InsufficientLiquidity()` (selector 0xbb55fd27, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:949) is returned as ABI custom error data when: A gross output above the spendable reserves or above spendable x maxUtilizationBps / 10000 of the output token (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:450 gross check; the cap is defined by this contract), a deposit into a pool with supply above zero and NAV 0, and a withdraw above the spendable reserves (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:80)."
ac_13 = "The liquidity check compares the gross output, before fee and impact, with the spendable book and the utilization cap of the output token, so a trade whose net fits but whose gross does not reverts InsufficientLiquidity()."

[req.4006]
title = "Swaps, native swaps and multicall run on 0x1021"
ac_1 = "swapExactIn and swapExactOut accept any two registered tokens, stable or not, and price them through the index prices of both (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:256-322)."
ac_2 = "multicall is served nonpayable as the source declares it (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:589-605), runs its elements in order in-process with one caller and returns each result; a failing element reverts the whole call, and one that fails without data reverts MulticallFailed(uint256) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:601); feature 6 changes the application ABI entry (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:404) from view to nonpayable."
ac_3 = "A plain value transfer to 0x1021 or 0x1025 reverts, so native PAX never sits unaccounted in a spot address (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:608-610, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/vault/PECORVault.sol:442-444)."
ac_4 = "PECOR `swapExactIn(address tokenIn, address tokenOut, uint256 amountIn, uint256 amountOutMin, uint256 deadline) returns (uint256 amountOut)` (0x55a124be, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:600): Pulls amountIn of tokenIn (ERC20 by transferFrom against an allowance to this rail, native by bank send), pays the net tokenOut output, emits SimpleSwap; SameToken(), ZeroAmount(), Expired(), InsufficientOutput(), InsufficientLiquidity() on a gross output above the spendable book or its utilization cap, as the engine (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:256-288)."
ac_5 = "PECOR `swapExactOut(address tokenIn, address tokenOut, uint256 amountOut, uint256 amountInMax, uint256 deadline) returns (uint256 amountIn)` (0x3cc75fd4, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:702): Prices the smallest input for amountOut, reverts ExcessiveInput() above amountInMax, pulls exactly that input (ERC20 by transferFrom against an allowance to this rail, native by bank send; a receipt other than the exact input reverts UnsupportedInputTransfer(), Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:307), pays amountOut and reserves the retained output as fees; emits SimpleSwap and no fee event (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:291-322)."
ac_6 = "PECOR `swapExactInNative(address tokenOut, uint256 amountOutMin, uint256 deadline) returns (uint256 amountOut)` (0xbac7a125, payable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:639): Payable: takes the attached value as uhpx at value / 1e12, prices it as PAX and pays tokenOut; tokenOut equal to the PAX pointer reverts UseWethDeposit(); emits NativeSwap with nativeIsInput true (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:407-455)."
ac_7 = "PECOR `swapExactInToNative(address tokenIn, uint256 amountIn, uint256 amountOutMin, uint256 deadline) returns (uint256 amountOut)` (0xce9e0cae, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:668): Pulls tokenIn from the caller (ERC20 by transferFrom against an allowance to this rail, native by bank send), prices the output as PAX and pays it as uhpx to the caller by bank send; tokenIn equal to the PAX pointer reverts UseWethWithdraw(); emits NativeSwap with nativeIsInput false (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:458-502)."
ac_8 = "PECOR `multicall(bytes[] data) returns (bytes[] results)` (0xac9650d8, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:404): Runs each element against 0x1021 with the same caller in order; the first failing element reverts the whole call with its own revert data, or MulticallFailed(index) when it has none (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:589-605, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:601). Served nonpayable as the source; feature 6 changes the application ABI entry from view to nonpayable."
ac_9 = "PECOR `receive() external payable` ((no selector), payable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:33): A plain value transfer to 0x1021 reverts NativeTransferFailed(); native input enters only through swapExactInNative (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:608-610)."
ac_10 = "The event `SimpleSwap(address indexed user, address indexed tokenIn, address indexed tokenOut, uint256 amountIn, uint256 amountOut, uint256 executionPrice)` (topic0 0x1075e5ad13b06b3fb5457eb645716bfaea9f0117bfefda8d940bf2b926b41c1f, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:995) is written at 0x1021 by: swapExactIn and swapExactOut at 0x1021; executionPrice is the tokenOut index price (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:286, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:320)."
ac_11 = "The event `NativeSwap(address indexed user, address indexed tokenOther, uint256 nativeAmount, uint256 tokenAmount, bool nativeIsInput)` (topic0 0xab06313637ec959a5d89f14a6be0f060979206219814eee5ed4d74dc7525ba20, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:895) is written at 0x1021 by: swapExactInNative (nativeIsInput true) and swapExactInToNative (nativeIsInput false) at 0x1021 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:453, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:500)."
ac_12 = "The error `SameToken()` (selector 0x201b580a, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:1051) is returned as ABI custom error data when: tokenIn equal to tokenOut on a swap or quote (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:263)."
ac_13 = "The error `ExcessiveInput()` (selector 0xbd750b82, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:79) is returned as ABI custom error data when: swapExactOut whose required input exceeds amountInMax (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:305)."
ac_14 = "The error `UseWethDeposit()` (selector 0xb1da5593, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:83) is returned as ABI custom error data when: swapExactInNative with tokenOut the PAX pointer (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:423)."
ac_15 = "The error `UseWethWithdraw()` (selector 0x74ee4e2a, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:84) is returned as ABI custom error data when: swapExactInToNative with tokenIn the PAX pointer (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:474)."
ac_16 = "The error `NativeTransferFailed()` (selector 0xf4b3b1bc, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:89) is returned as ABI custom error data when: A plain value transfer to 0x1021, or a PAX payout that the recipient refuses (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:608-610)."
ac_17 = "The error `MulticallFailed(uint256)` (selector 0x750ebb7d, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:90) is returned as ABI custom error data when: A multicall element that fails without revert data (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:601)."
ac_18 = "The error `UnsupportedInputTransfer()` (selector 0x1c42e5ce, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:91) is returned as ABI custom error data when: An ERC20 receipt that differs from the exact input of swapExactOut (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:307), and an attached value that is not a whole multiple of 1e12 wei, so it does not convert to whole uhpx (the exact-input rule of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:429)."

[req.4007]
title = "PECOR quotes match the executed trade"
ac_1 = "getQuoteExactIn returns exactly the net output a swapExactIn of the same input would pay in the same block."
ac_2 = "getDetailedQuote returns grossOut, netOut, priceImpactBps, feeBps and feeAmount from one evaluation of the pricing formula (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:540-583)."
ac_3 = "A quote never writes state and runs under eth_call with zero value."
ac_4 = "PECOR `getQuoteExactIn(address tokenIn, address tokenOut, uint256 amountIn) returns (uint256 amountOut)` (0x8063c834, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:242): Returns the net output of amountIn by the pricing formula (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:505-524)."
ac_5 = "PECOR `getQuoteExactOut(address tokenIn, address tokenOut, uint256 amountOut) returns (uint256 amountIn)` (0x08fedc90, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:271): Returns the smallest input whose net output is at least amountOut, searched per fee tier (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:527-537, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:648-686); SameToken() and ZeroAmount() as the engine."
ac_6 = "PECOR `getDetailedQuote(address tokenIn, address tokenOut, uint256 amountIn) returns (uint256 grossOut, uint256 netOut, uint256 priceImpactBps, uint256 feeBps, uint256 feeAmount)` (0xbfee15f8, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:193): Returns grossOut, netOut, priceImpactBps, feeBps and feeAmount for amountIn by the pricing formula, without state change (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:540-583)."

[req.4008]
title = "PECOR configuration is governed by the spot module parameters"
ac_1 = "Every PECOR setter, pause, unpause, renounceOwnership and transferOwnership reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) for every EVM caller; the values change only through MsgUpdateParams signed by the governance authority, checked as launchpad checks it (modules/launchpad/keeper/keeper.go:76-86)."
ac_2 = "Params.Validate refuses swapFeeBps + tier1FeeBps + tier2FeeBps above MAX_FEE_BPS 200 (FeeTooHigh), tier2FeeBps below tier1FeeBps (Tier2BelowTier1) and priceImpactScalarBps above MAX_IMPACT_BPS 500 (ScalarTooHigh) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:187-216), and for the order pricing set the bounds of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:502-509."
ac_3 = "A parameter change that flips swapPaused emits Paused or Unpaused at 0x1021 with account the governance module EVM address; a change of the TWAP sanity triple emits TwapSanityUpdated."
ac_4 = "collectFees pays the swap-rail accrual to feeCollector only when the caller is feeCollector (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:246-253)."
ac_5 = "PECOR `owner() returns (address)` (0x8da5cb5b, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:423): Returns the EVM address of the governance module account, the only authority over spot parameters (modules/launchpad/keeper/keeper.go:76-86 pattern)."
ac_6 = "PECOR `renounceOwnership()` (0x715018a6, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:482): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams."
ac_7 = "PECOR `transferOwnership(address newOwner)` (0xf2fde38b, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:793): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams."
ac_8 = "PECOR `pause()` (0x8456cb59, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:436): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams (swapPaused) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:232-236)."
ac_9 = "PECOR `unpause()` (0x3f4ba83a, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:832): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams (swapPaused) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:238-240)."
ac_10 = "PECOR `paused() returns (bool)` (0x5c975abb, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:443): Returns the swapPaused parameter; while true every swap and market method reverts EnforcedPause()."
ac_11 = "PECOR `setSwapFee(uint256 _feeBps)` (0x34e19907, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:533): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams; Params.Validate refuses a fee stack above 200 with FeeTooHigh() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:187-191)."
ac_12 = "PECOR `setTieredFees(uint256 _tier1FeeBps, uint256 _tier2FeeBps)` (0xf4b14e72, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:546): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams; Params.Validate refuses tier2 below tier1 with Tier2BelowTier1() and a stack above 200 with FeeTooHigh() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:196-205)."
ac_13 = "PECOR `setPriceImpact(bool _enabled, uint256 _scalarBps)` (0x646f23a8, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:502): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams; Params.Validate refuses a scalar above MAX_IMPACT_BPS 500 with ScalarTooHigh() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:212)."
ac_14 = "PECOR `setTwapSanity(bool enabled, uint256 period, uint256 maxDeviationBps_)` (0x8bd73d2d, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:577): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams (twapSanityEnabled, twapSanityPeriod, maxTwapDeviationBps); a change emits TwapSanityUpdated."
ac_15 = "PECOR `twapSanityEnabled() returns (bool)` (0x7b73a632, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:806): Returns the twapSanityEnabled parameter."
ac_16 = "PECOR `twapSanityPeriod() returns (uint256)` (0x09472882, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:819): Returns the twapSanityPeriod parameter in seconds."
ac_17 = "PECOR `maxTwapDeviationBps() returns (uint256)` (0x51e80e86, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:391): Returns the maxTwapDeviationBps parameter of the TWAP sanity rule (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/oracle/PriceOracle.sol:183-206)."
ac_18 = "PECOR `setPriceOracle(address _oracle)` (0x530e784f, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:520): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams; the oracle is fixed at 0x1020 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:173)."
ac_19 = "PECOR `setTransactionTracker(address _tracker)` (0xd25a18e5, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:564): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams; no tracker is configured (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:180)."
ac_20 = "PECOR `transactionTracker() returns (address)` (0xa4cf2f1c, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:780): Returns the zero address; trade records are the logs of this contract (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:98)."
ac_21 = "PECOR `vault() returns (address)` (0xfbfa77cf, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:839): Returns 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001025 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:97)."
ac_22 = "PECOR `feeCollector() returns (address)` (0xc415b95c, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:161): Returns the feeCollector parameter (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:116)."
ac_23 = "PECOR `setFeeCollector(address _collector)` (0xa42dce80, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:489): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams; Params.Validate refuses the zero address with ZeroAddress() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:220-229)."
ac_24 = "PECOR `accumulatedFees(address) returns (uint256)` (0xfcf66664, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:129): Returns the swap-rail fee accrual of the token, kept reserved in the vault (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:120)."
ac_25 = "PECOR `getAccumulatedFees(address token) returns (uint256)` (0x564201f9, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:174): Same value as accumulatedFees(token) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:120)."
ac_26 = "PECOR `collectFees(address token)` (0xa480ca79, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:148): Pays the whole swap-rail accrual of token to feeCollector, zeroes it and releases its reservation; a caller other than feeCollector reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller), the ABI form of the source FEE_COLLECTOR_ROLE check; a zero accrual reverts NoFeesToCollect() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:246-253)."
ac_27 = "The event `OwnershipTransferred(address indexed previousOwner, address indexed newOwner)` (topic0 0x8be0079c531659141344cd1fd0a4f28419497f9722a3daafe3b4186f6b6457e0, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:932) is written at 0x1021, 0x1022, 0x1023, 0x1025, share pointer by: Once per rail address at activation by InitV6120, in the activation synthetic receipt; the share pointer has no Ownable and never emits it; previous address(0), new the governance module EVM address; never again, the authority being fixed."
ac_28 = "The event `Paused(address account)` (topic0 0x62e78cea01bee320cd4e420270b5ea74000d11b0c9f74754ebdbfc544b05a258, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:951) is written at 0x1021, 0x1022, 0x1023 by: At 0x1021 when swapPaused turns true, at 0x1022 and 0x1023 when ordersPaused turns true; account is the governance module EVM address."
ac_29 = "The event `Unpaused(address account)` (topic0 0x5db9ee0a495bf2e6ff9c91a7834c1ba4fdd244a5e8aa4e537bd38aeae4b073aa, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:1100) is written at 0x1021, 0x1022, 0x1023 by: As Paused, when the flag turns false."
ac_30 = "The event `TwapSanityUpdated(bool enabled, uint256 period, uint256 maxDeviationBps)` (topic0 0x53c5e83e6ce0cd0796333da83f54e0738e25b57e301950baab492700fc969808, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:1075) is written at 0x1021 by: At 0x1021 when a parameter change alters twapSanityEnabled, twapSanityPeriod or maxTwapDeviationBps."
ac_31 = "The error `OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(address account)` (selector 0x118cdaa7, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:1134) is returned as ABI custom error data when: Every admin setter, pause, unpause, renounceOwnership and transferOwnership, setPecor, the vault operator methods pullTokens, pushTokens, updateReserves, registerToken, emergencyWithdraw, and collectFees on 0x1021 by a caller other than feeCollector; argument the caller."
ac_32 = "The error `OwnableInvalidOwner(address owner)` (selector 0x1e4fbdf7, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:1123) is returned as ABI custom error data when: Never produced: the authority is fixed to the governance module; listed for selector parity."
ac_33 = "The error `EnforcedPause()` (selector 0xd93c0665, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:1113) is returned as ABI custom error data when: A call to a paused rail: swaps and market orders while swapPaused, placement and execution while ordersPaused."
ac_34 = "The error `ExpectedPause()` (selector 0x8dfc202b, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:1118) is returned as ABI custom error data when: Never produced: pause state changes only through governance; listed for selector parity."
ac_35 = "The error `FeeTooHigh()` (selector 0xcd4e6167, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:86) is returned as ABI custom error data when: Params.Validate when swapFeeBps + tier1FeeBps + tier2FeeBps exceeds 200 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:187-205)."
ac_36 = "The error `Tier2BelowTier1()` (selector 0x305ea8a9, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:87) is returned as ABI custom error data when: Params.Validate when tier2FeeBps is below tier1FeeBps (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:196-205)."
ac_37 = "The error `ScalarTooHigh()` (selector 0xf4e307b5, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:88) is returned as ABI custom error data when: Params.Validate when priceImpactScalarBps or orderPriceImpactScalarBps exceeds MAX_IMPACT_BPS 500 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:212, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:505); a module error of MsgUpdateParams, never EVM revert data."
ac_38 = "The error `NoFeesToCollect()` (selector 0x6a4ea9e4, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:979) is returned as ABI custom error data when: collectFees with a zero accrual (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:248)."
ac_39 = "The error `ZeroAddress()` (selector 0xd92e233d, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:74) is returned as ABI custom error data when: Params.Validate for a zero feeCollector or keeper; InitV6120 for a zero token address (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:220-229)."
ac_40 = "Params.Validate refuses a zero EndBlock budget (maxExpiriesPerBlock, activationScanPerBlock, fillScanPerBlock or maxFillsPerBlock), a zero maxActiveOrdersPerUser, a zero maxFillBackoffBlocks, a maxUtilizationBps of 0 or above 10000 and a token without a kind; the UpdateParams handler also refuses a NATIVE token whose address is not a native pointer."

[req.4009]
title = "Limit orders rest in escrow and follow the order lifecycle"
ac_1 = "Placement validates every argument before any token move (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:226-229 and Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:249-254 run before the pulls at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:231 and Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:256), pulls the input into custody as escrow, records the order PENDING with a new id from the shared counter, appends it to the user list and the active index of its kind, and emits LimitOrderCreated (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:223-244)."
ac_2 = "Status moves only PENDING to EXECUTED, PENDING to CANCELLED or PENDING to EXPIRED for limit orders on 0x1022, with the status values of the order enum (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/interfaces/IPECOROrders.sol:22-28); 0x1022 holds no STOP_LOSS order."
ac_3 = "An escrow is reserved: it never counts as spendable reserves and leaves custody only as the fill input or the refund (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/vault/PECORVault.sol:541-550)."
ac_4 = "A filled, cancelled or expired order leaves the active list by swap and pop (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:643-655) and stays readable by id."
ac_5 = "PECOROrders `placeLimitBuy(address stablecoin, address token, uint256 stablecoinAmount, uint256 targetPrice, uint256 expiresAt) returns (uint256 orderId)` (0x947de5b1, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:526): Pulls stablecoinAmount into escrow (ERC20 by transferFrom against an allowance to this rail, native by bank send), records a LIMIT_BUY order with targetPrice in USD per whole token, emits LimitOrderCreated (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:192-194, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:223-244)."
ac_6 = "PECOROrders `placeLimitSell(address token, address stablecoin, uint256 tokenAmount, uint256 targetPrice, uint256 expiresAt) returns (uint256 orderId)` (0x31880832, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:565): Pulls tokenAmount into escrow (ERC20 by transferFrom against an allowance to this rail, native by bank send), records a LIMIT_SELL order, emits LimitOrderCreated (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:196-198, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:223-244)."
ac_7 = "PECOROrders `cancelLimitOrder(uint256 orderId)` (0xa5cdc8fc, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:155): Refunds the escrow of a pending limit order to its user and marks it CANCELLED; a caller other than the user reverts NotOrderOwner(); a status other than PENDING reverts CannotCancel(), the ABI name of the source OrderNotPending() of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:566; emits LimitOrderCancelled (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:270-272, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:565-579)."
ac_8 = "PECOROrders `modifyLimitOrder(uint256 orderId, uint256 newTargetPrice, uint256 newExpiresAt)` (0x3f08abf2, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:444): Changes targetPrice and expiresAt of the caller's pending limit order without touching the escrow; NotOrderOwner(), OrderNotPending(), InvalidPrice() for a zero target, InvalidExpiry() for a past non-zero expiry; emits LimitOrderModified (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:351-359)."
ac_9 = "PECOROrders `executeLimitOrder(uint256 orderId)` (0xc7219460, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:181): Fills one pending limit order at the current index price by the execution rule; a stop-loss id or a final order reverts OrderNotPending() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:412), OrderExpired() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:413), PriceAboveTarget() and PriceBelowTarget() (the ABI names of the source PriceNotMet() of Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:417-418), InsufficientOutput(), InsufficientLiquidity(); emits LimitOrderExecuted (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:279-282, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:410-429)."
ac_10 = "PECOROrders `batchExecuteLimitOrders(uint256[] orderIds) returns (uint256 executedCount)` (0xa188c99c, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:93): Tries each id as executeLimitOrder in isolation; an id that cannot fill is skipped without revert; returns the number filled (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:310-319)."
ac_11 = "PECOROrders `batchExpireOrders(uint256[] orderIds) returns (uint256 expiredCount)` (0xfe749155, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:112): Expires and refunds every listed limit order whose expiresAt is non-zero and not after the block time, emitting LimitOrderExpired for each; other ids, stop-limit and stop-loss ids included, are skipped; returns the number expired (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:538-545, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:573)."
ac_12 = "The event `LimitOrderCreated(uint256 indexed orderId, address indexed user, uint8 orderType, uint256 amount, uint256 targetPrice)` (topic0 0x7df754202cad14218ee77bcea0466d971b8145466b889f56634e2e8e66d17404, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:790) is written at 0x1022 by: placeLimitBuy and placeLimitSell at 0x1022, orderType 0 or 1 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:239)."
ac_13 = "The event `LimitOrderCancelled(uint256 indexed orderId)` (topic0 0xa79034042a790ce528ef3275727fa99fa364bebccd18f9d6094e524e8c075f86, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:777) is written at 0x1022 by: cancelLimitOrder at 0x1022 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:579)."
ac_14 = "The event `LimitOrderExecuted(uint256 indexed orderId, uint256 executionPrice)` (topic0 0x8473464af225412ba591d2bcb9cbddb9456a28347037e7fd76b14ef834e7caff, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:827) is written at 0x1022 by: A limit fill (never a stop-loss fill), from executeLimitOrder or the batch method in the transaction receipt, or from EndBlock in the spot synthetic receipt, at 0x1022 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:423)."
ac_15 = "The event `LimitOrderExpired(uint256 indexed orderId)` (topic0 0xdf3c7dca4ba1afef3742d2720d6e060c9abc5bfcfcaa653ee459d8b22ae17217, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:846) is written at 0x1022 by: Expiry of a limit order by batchExpireOrders or the EndBlock sweep, at 0x1022; it replaces the source OrderExpiredAndRefunded (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:576) for limit orders."
ac_16 = "The event `LimitOrderModified(uint256 indexed orderId, uint256 targetPrice, uint256 expiresAt)` (topic0 0x4faf905c59d1d8f751a461274695b2985d465bc0ab5818e8c53e12c6973085c1, Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:859) is written at 0x1022 by: modifyLimitOrder at 0x1022."
ac_17 = "An order whose escrow value at the index price is below minOrderNotional reverts OrderBelowMinimumNotional() before any token move."
ac_18 = "A user who already has maxActiveOrdersPerUser active orders across the three kinds reverts TooManyActiveOrders() at placement; a cancel, fill or expiry frees a slot."
ac_19 = "Each order keeps orderMinOutput (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:113, set at Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:238 and Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:263), 0 for every placement through the application selectors, as the source placement entry points pass 0 (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:192-210); a fill whose net output is below it, or zero, reverts InsufficientOutput() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:449) and leaves the order PENDING."
ac_20 = "The error `OrderBelowMinimumNotional()` (selector 0x9b2bea5b, contracts/spot.md#added-error-entries) is returned as ABI custom error data when: An order placement whose escrow value at the index price is below minOrderNotional; defined by contracts/spot.md#order-lifecycle."
ac_21 = "The error `TooManyActiveOrders()` (selector 0x28d7a641, contracts/spot.md#added-error-entries) is returned as ABI custom error data when: An order placement by a user who already has maxActiveOrdersPerUser active orders across the three kinds; defined by contracts/spot.md#order-lifecycle."
ac_22 = "Anyone may expire a limit order whose non-zero expiresAt is at or before the block time (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:538-545); it becomes EXPIRED, its escrow returns to its user, it leaves the active index and the expiry index, the active count of its user falls by one, and LimitOrderExpired is written at 0x1022."

[req.4010]
title = "Limit order views read the stored records"
ac_1 = "getExecutableLimitOrders scans the active list in order and returns at most 100 ids for which canExecuteLimitOrder is true (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrderViews.sol:116-147)."
ac_2 = "canExecuteLimitOrder returns the first failing reason string of the engine views in their order (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrderViews.sol:78-115)."
ac_3 = "An unknown id reads as the zero record, never a revert."
ac_4 = "PECOROrders `getLimitOrder(uint256 orderId) returns ((uint256 id, address user, address stablecoin, address token, uint256 amount, uint256 targetPrice, uint8 orderType, uint8 status, uint256 createdAt, uint256 expiresAt))` (0x53061026, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:271): Returns the LimitOrder record; an unknown id returns the zero record (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:341-343, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/interfaces/IPECOROrders.sol:45-56)."
ac_5 = "PECOROrders `limitOrders(uint256) returns (uint256 id, address user, address stablecoin, address token, uint256 amount, uint256 targetPrice, uint8 orderType, uint8 status, uint256 createdAt, uint256 expiresAt)` (0xa3e2b495, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:380): Returns the LimitOrder fields as a flat tuple (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:97)."
ac_6 = "PECOROrders `getUserLimitOrders(address user) returns (uint256[])` (0xdd5d02e6, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:342): Returns every limit id the user placed, in placement order, stop-loss ids excluded (they are returned by getUserStopLossOrders at 0x1023) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:353-358)."
ac_7 = "PECOROrders `userLimitOrders(address, uint256) returns (uint256)` (0xa5bb2be6, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:740): Returns the id at position i of the user's limit list (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:99)."
ac_8 = "PECOROrders `activeLimitOrderIds(uint256) returns (uint256)` (0xb234ff4c, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:74): Returns the id at position i of the active limit list (limit buy and limit sell only; stop-loss ids live in the index of 0x1023), swap-and-pop on removal (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:102, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:643-655)."
ac_9 = "PECOROrders `getActiveLimitOrderCount() returns (uint256)` (0xbf2badf0, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:239): Returns the length of the active limit list (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:366-368)."
ac_10 = "PECOROrders `getExecutableLimitOrders(uint256 maxCount) returns (uint256[] orderIds)` (0x4ef735de, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:252): Returns up to min(maxCount, 100) active ids for which canExecuteLimitOrder is true, in list order (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:389-391, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrderViews.sol:116-147)."
ac_11 = "PECOROrders `canExecuteLimitOrder(uint256 orderId) returns (bool, string)` (0xf16c867f, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:131): Returns (true, \"Executable\") or false with the first failing reason of the engine views: \"Order not found\", \"Order not pending\", \"Paused\", \"Order expired\", \"Price unavailable\", \"Price above target\", \"Price below target\", \"Price above trigger\", \"Escrow deficit\", \"Insufficient output\", \"Insufficient liquidity\" (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrderViews.sol:78-115)."

[req.4011]
title = "Resting limit and stop orders execute in EndBlock against the pool price"
ac_1 = "The spot EndBlocker runs in the legacy end block in the order oracle, perps, spot, EVM (baseline task 1.3.103), and the pricefeed aggregates in MidBlock (baseline task 1.3.100), so the index read is the one of the current block; required change for the baseline wiring task 1.3.100: EndBlockKeepers (node/legacyabci/end_block.go:15-20) carries the spot keeper and EndBlock calls spot.EndBlocker (node/legacyabci/end_block.go:22-28)."
ac_2 = "Each block runs, in order: one TWAP sample per registered non-stable token; at most maxExpiriesPerBlock (default 200) expiries from the expiry index ordered by (expiresAt, id); an activation scan of at most activationScanPerBlock (default 500) PENDING stop-limits; and a fill scan of at most fillScanPerBlock (default 500) entries over the activated stop-limits, the limit index and the stop-loss index, with at most maxFillsPerBlock (default 200) fills."
ac_3 = "Each fill runs in its own cached context; a fill that fails (stale price, liquidity, fill-quality hold, output below the order minimum, token transfer) writes nothing but its back-off record: the failure count rises and the next-retry height becomes the current height + min(2^failures, maxFillBackoffBlocks), default 256; scans skip the order until that height, and a fill, cancel or expiry deletes the record."
ac_4 = "The activation and fill scans resume at persisted cursors and wrap at the end of their index, so every active order is examined within ceil(index length / budget) blocks, and the EndBlock work of one block is bounded by the sum of the budgets whatever the number of active orders."
ac_5 = "The EndBlocker runs under SyntheticReceiptContext(ctx, SyntheticReceiptSpot) of baseline task 1.0.6, the receipt whose hash is keccak256(\"spot-endblock\" || height as 8 big-endian bytes) and whose TransactionIndex is the highest real index + 2; the USDL Transfer logs of CallEVM merge into it (modules/evm/keeper/evm.go:130-153), the spot logs are appended through GetTransientReceipt and SetTransientReceipt (modules/evm/keeper/receipt.go:28-38), each converted by ConvertSyntheticEthLog (modules/evm/keeper/log.go:109), and task 1.0.6 serves the receipt through eth_getLogs, pax_getLogs, eth_getBlockReceipts, eth_getTransactionReceipt and the block bloom."
ac_6 = "The execute and batch methods on 0x1022 and 0x1023 apply the same rule inside a transaction, so a keeper can fill an order before EndBlock does; an order filled by a transaction is not filled again by EndBlock."
ac_7 = "While fillQualityTwapPeriod is non-zero, a fill whose index price deviates from the TWAP over that period by more than maxTwapDeviationBps is skipped for the block."
ac_8 = "With 10,000 PENDING stop-limits one EndBlock examines at most activationScanPerBlock of them for activation and fillScanPerBlock entries for fills, runs at most maxFillsPerBlock fills, and its activation cursor records where the next block resumes."

[req.4012]
title = "Order-rail configuration on 0x1022 and 0x1023 is shared and governed"
ac_1 = "0x1022 and 0x1023 read one parameter set: the order pricing set orderFeeBps, orderTier1FeeBps, orderTier2FeeBps, orderPriceImpactEnabled and orderPriceImpactScalarBps, keeperOpen, keepers, fillQualityTwapPeriod, ordersPaused and feeCollector, and one order-rail fee accrual (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:110-120)."
ac_2 = "While keeperOpen is true any account may call the execute and batch methods; while it is false only listed keepers may, and others revert NotAuthorized()."
ac_3 = "While ordersPaused is true placement and execution revert EnforcedPause() and cancellation succeeds, so a user can always recover an escrow."
ac_4 = "PECOROrders `owner() returns (address)` (0x8da5cb5b, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:493): Returns the EVM address of the governance module account, the only authority over spot parameters (modules/launchpad/keeper/keeper.go:76-86 pattern)."
ac_5 = "PECOROrders `renounceOwnership()` (0x715018a6, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:617): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams."
ac_6 = "PECOROrders `transferOwnership(address newOwner)` (0xf2fde38b, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:720): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams."
ac_7 = "PECOROrders `pause()` (0x8456cb59, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:506): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams (ordersPaused) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:182-185)."
ac_8 = "PECOROrders `unpause()` (0x3f4ba83a, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:733): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams (ordersPaused) (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:188-190)."
ac_9 = "PECOROrders `paused() returns (bool)` (0x5c975abb, view) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:513): Returns the ordersPaused parameter; while true placement and execution revert EnforcedPause() and cancellation stays open."
ac_10 = "PECOROrders `setKeeper(address keeper, bool authorized)` (0xd1b9e853, nonpayable) is served at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001022 with the application signature (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:650): Reverts OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller) (0x118cdaa7) for every EVM caller; the value changes only through governance MsgUpdateParams (keeperOpen, keepers); Params.Validate refuses the zero address with ZeroAddress() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOROrders.sol:167-179)."
