# Domain 6: the Hyperpax application trades against the perpetuals and spot precompiles and reads the gateway data services.

[feature.6]
name = "application"
scope = "The Hyperpax application resolves every chain call through one precompile address table (perpetuals 0x1015, launchpad 0x1017 as an allowance spender, spot 0x1021-0x1025), encodes with ABIs generated from the contract files including their typed custom errors, sends bounded perpetuals writes through placeOrder and closePositionWithParams with price bound, deadline, time in force, reduce-only and take-profit and stop-loss, uses six-decimal USDL amounts and exact ERC20 allowances to the precompile addresses with none for the native PAX and SID coins, holds one USDL cross-margin account read with an explicit account argument, trades spot on the spot precompile set with the uhpx and SID denom pointers and the PAX/USDL and SID/USDL markets, keeps charts, prices, candles and reference books on Chainflow, reads the gateway for the venue's own fills, book and account state and history over REST, WebSocket with snapshot resume and GraphQL with its existing operation set, sends every write with an estimated gas margin and a quoted confirmation, signs through the embedded wallet with a PKCE session, classifies precompile custom errors, declares its deploy configuration and completes the trading round trip against a local node at v6.12.0."
requirements = ["6001", "6002", "6003", "6004", "6005", "6006", "6007", "6008", "6009", "6010", "6011", "6012", "6013", "6014", "6015", "6016", "6017", "6018", "6019", "6020", "6021", "6022", "6023", "6024"]
completion_task = "6.3.99"

[req.6001]
title = "Every chain call of the application resolves through one precompile address table"
ac_1 = "The address module src/core/network/precompiles.ts (planned) exports the perpetuals precompile 0x1015, the launchpad precompile 0x1017 and the spot set 0x1021 to 0x1025 as 20-byte viem addresses, and DIAMOND_ADDRESS (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:10-11) is removed."
ac_2 = "Each address keeps the environment override pattern of envAddress (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/addresses.ts:23-27) under the variables NEXT_PUBLIC_PERPS_PRECOMPILE, NEXT_PUBLIC_LAUNCHPAD_PRECOMPILE and NEXT_PUBLIC_PECOR_*_PRECOMPILE, a value that is not a 20-byte hex address is refused at module load with the variable name, and the NEXT_PUBLIC_SPOT_* address overrides of Hyperpax:src/core/spot/addresses.ts:31-60 are removed."
ac_3 = "PECOR_CONTRACTS (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/addresses.ts:31-60) reads PECOR, PECORQuoter, PECOROrders, PECORStopOrders and PECORVault from the address module, and TransactionTracker (:52-55) and PriceOracle (:56-59) are removed; the application carries no oracle address or oracle ABI, because 0x1020 serves the pricefeed interface of contracts/pricefeed.md and the application has no call site for it."
ac_4 = "USDL is one address: the perpetuals collateral entry (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:75-79) and the spot USDL entry (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/addresses.ts:146-153) both read the existing six-decimal USDL ERC20 token of Launch-x:contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:14-16, 0x85FcD13735F4309833A503EE804ea32395851479; the PAX entry is the uhpx ERC20 native pointer and the SID entry the SID denom ERC20 native pointer that the baseline task \"Create the native ERC20 pointers and bank metadata for uhpx and the SID denom before venue activation\" records in contracts/address-table.md, and no WPAX9 address remains."
ac_5 = "No source file under src/ names the Diamond address or a PECOR contract address other than through the address module."
ac_6 = "The chain stays chain id 125 from paxeerChain (Hyperpax:src/core/chain.ts:16-17)."

[req.6002]
title = "The precompile ABIs are generated from the contract files and typed end to end"
ac_1 = "src/core/network/abi/PerpsPrecompile.ts (planned) is generated from contracts/perps.md in the as-const shape of Hyperpax:src/core/network/abi/PositionFacet.ts:1-2 and contains every method of the perpetual call-site and account tables of contracts/application.md, the OrderParams and PositionDetails tuples, the OrderType and TimeInForce enumerations, every event and every custom error of contracts/perps.md#19-errors, and the ABI test maps each of the 32 distinct 0x1015 methods the application calls today from usePosition.ts, usePerpsOrders.ts, useMarginMode.ts, useVault.ts, useQuoter.ts and usePortfolioStats.ts to its replacement or removal."
ac_2 = "The barrel Hyperpax:src/core/network/abi/index.ts:1-27 exports only the perpetuals precompile ABI and the token ABI, the Diamond facet ABI files are deleted, and no hook imports PositionFacetABI, OrderBookFacetABI, QuoterFacetABI, TradingAccountABI, VaultFactoryFacetABI or OracleFacetABI."
ac_3 = "The spot ABI files keep every selector the application encodes, for example marketBuy (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:313) and placeLimitBuy (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:526), carry every custom error contracts/spot.md lists for their rail, and a selector or error that differs from contracts/spot.md fails the golden test; the spot exports without a precompile (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/index.ts:4, :9-16) are deleted with their files."
ac_4 = "The call builders pass typed ABIs, so the params as any cast of readContract (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useContract.ts:8-16) never carries a precompile call and a signature drift fails pnpm tsc --noEmit."
ac_5 = "Reshaped views decode by output name from the regenerated ABI: getFees returns takerFeePpm, makerFeePpm, liquidationFeePpm and insuranceSharePpm read as parts per million, getMarkPriceDetails returns markPrice, indexPrice, midPrice and fresh, getFundingDetails returns its five named outputs, getLiquidationPrice takes a positionId, and the MarkPriceChanged record type of the Diamond indexer (Hyperpax:src/types/perps.ts:56) is read only through the gateway GraphQL schema, while on-chain event decoding uses the events of contracts/perps.md section 18."
ac_6 = "ORDER_TYPE_LABELS, ORDER_TYPE_COLORS, FEE_TYPE_LABELS and TRADE_TYPE_LABELS (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:212-217, :219-224, :262-267, :270-275) follow the numbering of contracts/perps.md section 2: ORDER_TYPE_LABELS and ORDER_TYPE_COLORS keep Limit 0, Stop-Limit 1, Take Profit 2 and Stop Loss 3 and gain Market 4 and Stop Market 5, TRADE_TYPE_LABELS keeps 0 to 3 and gains Increase 4, ADL 5 and Backstop 6, and FEE_TYPE_LABELS keeps Trading 0 and gains Maker Rebate 4."

[req.6003]
title = "Position calls go to the perpetuals precompile with their price bound and deadline"
ac_1 = "A market open (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:63-64) sends placeOrder(OrderParams) to 0x1015 with orderType MARKET, timeInForce IOC (FOK when chosen), marketId, isLong, collateral in USDL base units, leverage, acceptablePrice, deadline, takeProfitPrice and stopLossPrice; the fixed-arity openPosition of contracts/perps.md stays in the ABI."
ac_2 = "A bounded addSize (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:121-122) sends placeOrder with orderType MARKET and timeInForce IOC on the market and side of the position, with the added collateral in USDL base units, leverage at 18 decimals, acceptablePrice and deadline."
ac_3 = "closePosition (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:79-80) sends closePositionWithParams(positionId, closeSizeUsd, acceptablePrice, deadline) to 0x1015 with closeSizeUsd equal to the position size and acceptablePrice from the quoteClosePosition exitPrice."
ac_4 = "partialClose (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:89-90) sends closePositionWithParams with closeSizeUsd at 18 decimals and acceptablePrice from quotePartialClose, and the positions panel offers it beside handleClose (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsPositionsPanel.tsx:857-876)."
ac_5 = "addCollateral and removeCollateral (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:100-101, :110-111) target 0x1015 with the amount in USDL base units."
ac_6 = "getPosition, getUserPositionIds(account) and getOpenInterest (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:29-30, :38-39, :47-48) read 0x1015, and getPositionDetails(positionId) supplies take-profit, stop-loss and liquidation price."
ac_7 = "getPositionCollateralToken reads the collateral token by its output name instead of output index 5 (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:69-73)."

[req.6004]
title = "Order calls go to the perpetuals precompile with time in force, reduce-only and attached TP/SL"
ac_1 = "A limit order (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerpsOrders.ts:36-40) sends placeOrder with orderType LIMIT, marketId, isLong, triggerPrice, sizeUsd, leverage, collateral, timeInForce, reduceOnly, takeProfitPrice, stopLossPrice, deadline and cloid."
ac_2 = "A stop-limit order (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerpsOrders.ts:58-59) sends placeOrder with orderType STOP_LIMIT, the trigger and limit prices and the same fields."
ac_3 = "The take-profit / stop-loss of an open position (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerpsOrders.ts:81-82, :91-92; Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/modals/SetTpSlModal.tsx:84-91) is one setPositionTpSl(positionId, takeProfitPrice, stopLossPrice) call at 18 decimals, where 0 clears a side."
ac_4 = "cancelOrder (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerpsOrders.ts:71-72) targets 0x1015 and the positions panel cancel (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsPositionsPanel.tsx:885) uses it; a scaled ladder is cancelled rung by rung with cancelByCloid(marketId, cloid)."
ac_5 = "getOrder and getUserOrderIds(account) (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerpsOrders.ts:10-11, :19-20) read 0x1015."

[req.6005]
title = "Quotes come from Chainflow and the perpetuals precompile"
ac_1 = "The ticker and open interest of useQuoter stay on Chainflow MARKET_DATA_URL (imported as REST_API_URL at Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useQuoter.ts:4; reads at :54 and :82), and quoteMarket (:116-122) reads 0x1015 only after the ticker read fails."
ac_2 = "The fallback's maxLeverage and fixed maintenanceMarginBps (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useQuoter.ts:108-109) are replaced by the values quoteMarket returns."
ac_3 = "quoteOpenPosition and quoteClosePosition (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useQuoter.ts:126-140, :142-150) read 0x1015 and their entryPrice and exitPrice outputs feed the price bound."
ac_4 = "quotePartialClose(positionId, closeSizeUsd) returning exitPrice, closedPnl, fee and estimatedPayout (contracts/perps.md section 17) is read before a partial close and its exitPrice feeds the bound."

[req.6006]
title = "Collateral is a USDL cross-margin account held by the perpetuals precompile"
ac_1 = "deposit and withdraw (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useVault.ts:44-62) target 0x1015 instead of a per-user vault through src/hooks/perps/useAccount.ts (planned); the first deposit opens the account, the application sends no createVault, and useVault.ts with getVaultAddress and createVault (:8-24) is removed."
ac_2 = "Every account view passes the connected address explicitly: getAccount(account) (contracts/perps.md section 3) and the account-argument forms of getBalance, getLockedBalance and getAccountSummary that feature 3 adds, read directly at 0x1015; the Multicall3 aggregate (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePortfolioStats.ts:16, :153-161) is removed."
ac_3 = "topUpPosition (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useMarginMode.ts:147-178) targets 0x1015 with USDL base units; useTransferMargin (:180-211), TransferMarginModal with its import, action and mount (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsPositionsPanel.tsx:34, :514, :1240) and its copy (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:362, :371, :376) are removed, and transferMargin stays in the interface reverting CROSS_MARGIN_ONLY with no application caller."
ac_4 = "getAccountSummary and getPositionMargin (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useMarginMode.ts:96-145, :213-264) read 0x1015."
ac_5 = "Margin mode is cross: useMarginMode and useSetMarginMode (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useMarginMode.ts:15-94) are removed, MARGIN_MODE_LABELS (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:286-289) shows the cross label and the toggle (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsPositionsPanel.tsx:1008) is removed."
ac_6 = "useEmergencyWithdraw (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useMarginMode.ts:266-297) is removed and withdraw-all sends withdraw(USDL, getAccount(account).withdrawable)."
ac_7 = "COLLATERAL_TOKENS and COLLATERAL_OPTIONS (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:64-87) list USDL only."
ac_8 = "useAutoCollateral (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useAutoCollateral.ts:5, :36, :43) reads getAccount(account).collateral through the account hook instead of getVaultAddress and getBalance, and its fallback entry (:76, :90-91) is USDL at 6 decimals."

[req.6007]
title = "Every on-chain amount uses the decimals of its unit"
ac_1 = "AdjustCollateralModal converts add-collateral, remove-collateral and add-size collateral with six decimals instead of parseEther (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/modals/AdjustCollateralModal.tsx:68, :81, :86) and keeps leverage at 18 decimals."
ac_2 = "TopUpPositionModal (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/modals/TopUpPositionModal.tsx:39) converts with six decimals, and the modal conversions live in the pure module src/core/perps/collateralInputs.ts (planned)."
ac_3 = "DepositWithdrawModal converts with safeParseUnits (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/amounts.ts:26-38) instead of BigInt(Math.floor(num * 10 ** decimals)) (Hyperpax:src/app/modals/DepositWithdrawModal.tsx:198)."
ac_4 = "getCollateralDecimals throws for an unknown token instead of returning 18 (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/amounts.ts:40-45)."
ac_5 = "Prices, sizeUsd and leverage stay at 18 decimals as the form converts them (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:327-348), with sub-1x leverage refused."
ac_6 = "The spot stable decimals come from the market's quote token metadata instead of the fixed decimalsStable = 6 (Hyperpax:src/widgets/spot/SpotOrderForm.tsx:418)."

[req.6008]
title = "ERC20 allowances to the precompile addresses request exactly the amount of the call they precede"
ac_1 = "needsApproval(token, allowance, amount) returns false for the PAX and SID pointers and native value and otherwise true only when allowance < amount, and the MAX_UINT256 / 2 threshold (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotApprovals.ts:40, :139) is removed."
ac_2 = "A short allowance is raised through approveExact (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotApprovals.ts:87-100) for exactly the amount, never approveMax (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotApprovals.ts:67-79, :143)."
ac_3 = "The perpetuals allowance step replacing ensureDiamondAllowance (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:13-22) and the deposit check of DepositWithdrawModal (Hyperpax:src/app/modals/DepositWithdrawModal.tsx:203-204) use spender 0x1015 for USDL."
ac_4 = "The spot rails approve an ERC20 input to 0x1021 for market orders, 0x1022 for limit orders and 0x1023 for stop orders (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:151-156, :288-293), and the spender table lists 0x1017 for the launchpad."
ac_5 = "No approval requested by the application exceeds the amount of its call or equals 2^256 - 1."
ac_6 = "No allowance is read or requested for the PAX or SID pointer or for native value, because the precompiles move those coins by bank transfer."

[req.6009]
title = "Time in force and order options reach the precompile or are removed"
ac_1 = "The perpetuals form maps ioc, fok and postOnly (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:291-293) to timeInForce IOC, FOK and POST_ONLY; none of them is GTC on a limit or stop-limit order and IOC on a market order."
ac_2 = "IOC, FOK and post-only are mutually exclusive: post-only clears IOC and FOK, which already exclude each other (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:1084-1085)."
ac_3 = "reduceOnly (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:290) is sent as reduceOnly on limit and stop-limit orders."
ac_4 = "The hidden toggle (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:295, :1088) is removed and orderConfirm (:294) opens the confirmation step of req 6.23 before signing."
ac_5 = "A spot limit order with IOC or FOK (Hyperpax:src/widgets/spot/SpotOrderForm.tsx:421-427) takes its minimum output from the limit price through expectedOutFromPrice (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/slippage.ts:160), so a buy never pays above its limit."
ac_6 = "Spot post-only keeps forcing GTC (Hyperpax:src/widgets/spot/SpotOrderForm.tsx:367) and the spot reduce-only toggle (Hyperpax:src/widgets/spot/SpotOrderForm.tsx:207, :816) is removed."
ac_7 = "A market order never encodes GTC, because a MARKET order with GTC reverts INVALID_TIME_IN_FORCE (contracts/perps.md section 5) and an omitted field encodes 0."

[req.6010]
title = "Take-profit and stop-loss entered in the form are carried to the precompile"
ac_1 = "With tpslEnabled (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:234) the market branch sends tpPrice and slPrice (:235-236) as takeProfitPrice and stopLossPrice in the placeOrder call, which the call at :482 omits today."
ac_2 = "The limit and stop-limit branches (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:486, :490) send the same two fields; an unset price is 0."
ac_3 = "A long requires stopLossPrice below the reference price below takeProfitPrice and a short the mirror; a failing pair blocks submit with TRADE_TP_SL_INVALID (Hyperpax:src/core/errors/classify.ts:251-253)."
ac_4 = "SetTpSlModal (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/modals/SetTpSlModal.tsx:84-91) sends one setPositionTpSl(positionId, takeProfitPrice, stopLossPrice) for an open position at 18 decimals instead of a separate take-profit and stop-loss order."
ac_5 = "A position opened with TP and SL reads back with both prices attached through getPositionDetails(positionId)."

[req.6011]
title = "Every market-priced perpetuals write carries a price bound and a deadline"
ac_1 = "acceptablePrice for a market open or bounded addSize is entryPrice * (10000 + bps) / 10000 for a long and entryPrice * (10000 - bps) / 10000 for a short with bps = DEFAULT_SLIPPAGE_BPS (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:354)."
ac_2 = "Close and partial-close bounds use the quoted exitPrice with the opposite rounding."
ac_3 = "deadline is the reference block timestamp plus DEFAULT_MARKET_DEADLINE_SECONDS (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/slippage.ts:27) built with buildDeadline (:75)."
ac_4 = "An aged quote (QUOTE_MAX_AGE_MS, Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:178) is re-fetched and the bound recomputed instead of blocking submit."
ac_5 = "Every bound is a bigint at 18 decimals computed with integer arithmetic only."

[req.6012]
title = "The order form submits through one pure order plan"
ac_1 = "src/core/perps/orderPlan.ts (planned) returns the ordered call list for market, limit, stop-limit and scaled orders and handleSubmit (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:444-506) submits exactly that list."
ac_2 = "A scaled order reads scaledStartPrice, scaledEndPrice, scaledTotalOrders and scaledDistribution (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:227-231) and returns N placeOrder calls with orderType LIMIT at evenly spaced prices from start to end inclusive, rung i carrying the cloid of the ladder id and i."
ac_3 = "Ascending and descending distributions weight rung i by i+1 and N-i and the integer remainder goes to the last rung."
ac_4 = "The custom distribution (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:29) has no input and returns no calls; fewer than 2 or more than 20 rungs return no calls."
ac_5 = "After a successful submit the form clears the inputs and the chart order lines together."

[req.6013]
title = "The spot widgets trade on the spot precompile set"
ac_1 = "marketBuy and marketSell (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:163-168, :253-258) target 0x1021 with their argument lists unchanged."
ac_2 = "placeLimitBuy, placeLimitSell, cancelLimitOrder, modifyLimitOrder, getUserLimitOrders and getLimitOrder (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:280-381) target 0x1022."
ac_3 = "placeStopLimitBuy, placeStopLimitSell, cancelStopLimitOrder, placeStopLoss, cancelStopLossOrder and the four stop readers (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:402-571) target 0x1023."
ac_4 = "Every quoter read (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotQuoter.ts:141-286) targets 0x1024 and the 23-field QuoteResult parse is unchanged."
ac_5 = "No wrap exists: the WPAX9 deposit before a sell (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:213-232) and its imports (:35-41) are removed; a PAX sell passes the uhpx pointer as the token of marketSell, which moves bank uhpx with no allowance, and a sell paid from native value calls swapExactInNative with value = amount x 1e12 wei (contracts/spot.md); the spot deadline semantics (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:132-135) are unchanged."
ac_6 = "The spot route gate (Hyperpax:src/pages/spot.tsx:2-3) asserted by Hyperpax:tests/audit-regressions.test.ts:7-11 stays as tested until release task 8.4.18 replaces the first case of Hyperpax:tests/audit-regressions.test.ts:7-11 when it opens the route behind NEXT_PUBLIC_RELEASE_SPOT_OPEN."

[req.6014]
title = "The account data hooks read the gateway over REST"
ac_1 = "INDEXER_BASE_URL, SUBGRAPH_PROXY_BASE, GRAPHQL_URL, SUBGRAPH_WS_URL, REST_API_URL and WS_URL (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:23-25, :28-30, :33, :34-36) are removed; the legacy indexer order book poll (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/Orderbook.tsx:143-148; Hyperpax:src/widgets/mobile/MobileTradeView.tsx:122) is removed, and the venue book resync reads the gateway route /api/orderbook/<SYMBOL> (contracts/data-services.md section 24)."
