[capability.7.2.1]
title = "Head follower with parent-hash continuity and rewind"
reqs = ["7003.1", "7003.2", "7003.3", "7003.4", "7003.5", "7003.6", "7003.12", "7003.13", "7003.14", "7003.15"]
touches = ["platform/perps-data/internal/source/rpc.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/source/comet.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/source/follower.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/source/follower_test.go"]
tests = ["platform/perps-data/internal/source/follower_test.go"]
verification_contract = "go test -count=1 ./platform/perps-data/internal/source/ -run 'TestFollower'"
do_1 = "Copy EVMOptions, EVMSource, NewEVM, Head, FetchLogs, toLog, getBlock, callWithFallback, rankedIndices, markSuccess, markFailure, runHealthCheck and parseHexUint64 (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:21, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:53, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:76, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:182, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:204, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:346, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:376, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:410, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:499, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:528, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:541, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:552, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/evm.go:633) into internal/source/rpc.go as RPC, origin Launch-x core/indexer/internal/source (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."
do_2 = "RPC.Logs filters on the address set of contracts/data-services.md section 1: 0x1015, 0x1020, 0x1021 to 0x1025, every share pointer of the pointer set and the USDL contract 0x85FcD13735F4309833A503EE804ea32395851479, in the FetchOptions and FetchResult shapes of Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/source.go:30 and Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/source.go:43; 0x1026 and 0x1027 carry no code and are not read. Block, transaction and log indexes are filled by the node because the precompile adds only address, topics and data (precompiles/common/evm_events.go:32-38)."
do_3 = "Catch-up reads at most 500 blocks per eth_getLogs call, below MaxBlocksForLog 2000 and MaxLogNoBlock 10000 (rpc/config/config.go:195-196), and halves the range and retries when the node refuses a response for size (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."
do_4 = "Logs of end blocks and of the activation arrive in the synthetic receipts served by baseline task 1.0.6; Follower.checkSynthetic compares each against the table of section 1 (perps_endblock at the highest real TxIndex plus 1, spot_endblock plus 2, activation plus 3, hash keccak256 of the tag and the 8-byte height) and stops the follower with the height, the expected and the served values on a mismatch, storing nothing under a guessed key (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."
do_5 = "Comet reads, per height over PERPS_COMET_URLS with fallback, the CometBFT header route for the proposer (consensus/internal/rpc/core/routes.go:44, consensus/types/block.go:423), written to perps.blocks.proposer as upper-case hex, and the block_results route for finalize_block_events (consensus/internal/rpc/core/routes.go:48, consensus/rpc/coretypes/responses.go:93), passed to the pricefeed decoder (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."
do_6 = "Share pointer discovery is two-pass per block: pass one decodes the logs of 0x1025 and records each ShareTokenCreated, pass two fetches the logs of the pointers known after pass one; at start the pointer set is seeded from getRegisteredTokens() (0x14cbd993) and shareTokens(address) (0x96153f07) on 0x1025 (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."
do_7 = "Follower.Step polls the head every 100 ms with 10 ms jitter, the cadence of Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/committed.go:830, and for each next height fetches the block and its logs; it checks the parent hash against the stored perps.blocks row of height n-1 as Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/committed.go:1037 does (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."
do_8 = "On a parent-hash mismatch or a stored hash that differs at the same height (the conflict of Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/source/committed.go:648), Follower.rewind walks back to the highest height whose stored hash equals the node hash; the fork height is that height plus one, the first height whose stored hash differs. In one transaction it deletes every fact and projection row at and above the fork height, moves the cursor to the fork height minus one and enqueues one perps.<chain>.chain.rewind message carrying the fork height; perps.markets and perps.fee_config are never deleted (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."
do_9 = "Projections are rebuilt for the affected accounts and markets from the remaining facts in the same transaction, so a read after the rewind never mixes rows of two branches (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."
do_10 = "Add TestFollower with subtests follows_head, detects_parent_mismatch, rewinds_to_fork, publishes_rewind, rpc_fallback, synthetic_receipt_check, comet_header_and_results, two_pass_pointers and rewind_keeps_markets against the node named by PERPS_DATA_TEST_RPC and PERPS_DATA_TEST_COMET (a node started with make run-local-node, chain.mk:278) and the Postgres of PERPS_DATA_TEST_DATABASE_URL; the mismatch case writes a perps.blocks row with a different hash at a real height and asserts the rewind (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."

[capability.7.2.2]
title = "Decoder registry and the perpetuals event decoders"
reqs = ["7004.1", "7004.2", "7004.3", "7004.4", "7004.5", "7004.6", "7004.7", "7004.8", "7004.9", "7004.10", "7004.11", "7004.12", "7004.13", "7004.14", "7004.15", "7004.16", "7004.17", "7004.18", "7004.19", "7004.20", "7004.21", "7004.22", "7004.23", "7004.24", "7004.25", "7004.26", "7004.27", "7004.28", "7004.29", "7004.30", "7004.31", "7004.32", "7004.33", "7004.34", "7004.35", "7004.36"]
touches = ["platform/perps-data/internal/decode/registry.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/decode/perps.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/decode/perps_test.go"]
tests = ["platform/perps-data/internal/decode/perps_test.go"]
verification_contract = "go test -count=1 ./platform/perps-data/internal/decode/ -run 'TestPerpsDecoders'"
do_1 = "Copy Event, Decoder, NewDecoder, Decode, unpackArgs and humanize (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/decode.go:31, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/decode.go:43, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/decode.go:49, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/decode.go:58, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/decode.go:82, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/decode.go:165) with exactArgs and boundedValue (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/scalars.go:14, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/scalars.go:82) and DeduplicateRaw (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/dedup.go:17) into internal/decode/registry.go, origin Launch-x core/indexer/internal/decode (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."
do_2 = "Registry, NewRegistry and Registry.Decode (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/registry.go:149, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/registry.go:158, Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/decode/registry.go:322) key decoders by (address, topic0); a log of a venue address with an unknown topic0 is written to perps.raw_logs with decoded false and counted in perps_indexer_unknown_logs_total, never dropped (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."
do_3 = "perps.go registers the 30 events at 0x1015 of the decoding table of contracts/data-services.md section 6, the events contracts/perps.md section 18 lists as emitted, from the leaf ABI package precompiles/perps/abi of the same commit; no decoder exists for the events of contracts/perps.md section 25 that the release does not emit or for BorrowingFeeAccrued, whose logs go to raw_logs with failure_class unknown_topic."
do_4 = "Each decoder returns a typed row (TradeSettledRow, FillRow and so on) whose unsigned amount fields are decimal strings checked by bigint.ValidateRaw and whose signed fields (grossPnl, fundingPaidUsd, realizedPnl, makerFeeUsd, fundingRate, longPayment, shortPayment, newRatePerSecond, fundingRate24h, fundingPaymentUsd) by bigint.ValidateRawInt256; CollateralTransferred yields two rows, transferred_out with sub 0 and account from and transferred_in with sub 1 and account to (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."
do_5 = "The account column takes the argument named in section 6, the user of the earlier placed or opened row of the same id (from the rows of the same batch, else perps.order_events and perps.position_events) for events that carry only an id, and the venue module address otherwise; tx_from is the sender only for receipt_kind tx and never supplies the account, unlike the txFrom input of Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/processor/processor.go:337 (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."
do_6 = "tradeType decodes as 0 open, 1 close, 2 liquidation, 3 reduce, 4 increase, 5 adl, 6 backstop and feeType as 0 trading, 4 maker rebate, the numbering of contracts/perps.md section 2; feeType 1 to 3 is never emitted, and a value outside its enumeration (feeType 1 to 3 included) is stored as emitted and counted in perps_indexer_enum_unknown_total (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."
do_7 = "Add TestPerpsDecoders with one subtest per event of the 30 rows; each packs the arguments with the leaf ABI (abi.Arguments.Pack and abi.MakeTopics), decodes the resulting ethtypes.Log and asserts every column of the fact row, plus subtests unknown_topic, duplicate_log, account_rule, signed_columns, enum_unknown and not_emitted_events (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."

[capability.7.2.3]
title = "Spot, pricefeed and USDL event decoders"
reqs = ["7004.37", "7005.1", "7005.2", "7005.3", "7005.4", "7005.5", "7005.6", "7005.7", "7005.8", "7005.9", "7005.10", "7005.11", "7005.12", "7005.13", "7005.14", "7005.15", "7005.16", "7005.17", "7005.18", "7005.19", "7005.20", "7005.21", "7005.22", "7005.23", "7005.24", "7005.25", "7005.26", "7005.27", "7005.28", "7005.29", "7005.30", "7005.31", "7005.32", "7005.33", "7005.34", "7005.35", "7005.36", "7005.37", "7005.38", "7005.39", "7005.40", "7005.41", "7005.42", "7005.43", "7005.44", "7005.45", "7005.46", "7005.47", "7005.48", "7005.49", "7005.50", "7005.51"]
touches = ["platform/perps-data/internal/decode/spot.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/decode/pricefeed.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/decode/usdl.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/decode/abi_test.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/decode/spot_test.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/decode/pricefeed_test.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/decode/usdl_test.go"]
tests = ["platform/perps-data/internal/decode/abi_test.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/decode/spot_test.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/decode/pricefeed_test.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/decode/usdl_test.go"]
verification_contract = "go test -count=1 ./platform/perps-data/internal/decode/ -run 'TestSpotDecoders|TestPricefeedDecoders|TestUSDLDecoder|TestDecoderColumnsMatchABI'"
do_1 = "spot.go registers the spot rows of the decoding table of contracts/data-services.md section 6 at PECOR 0x1021, PECOROrders 0x1022, PECORStopOrders 0x1023, PECORVault 0x1025 and the share pointers, from the leaf ABI package precompiles/spot/abi of the same commit; PriceImpactApplied and TieredFeeApplied are matched by topic0 at any of 0x1021 to 0x1025, and no decoder exists for 0x1024 (view only, no logs), 0x1026 or 0x1027 (no code)."
do_2 = "The spot order events carry no token: the decoder resolves token and stablecoin by eth_call at the event height with getLimitOrder(uint256) (0x53061026) on 0x1022 and getStopLimitOrder(uint256) (0x307ff324) and getStopLossOrder(uint256) (0x4c34cf02) on 0x1023, calls the latest height when that height is pruned on every node, and writes a zero record to raw_logs with failure_class order_lookup; side is buy for limit orderType 0, sell for 1, and sell for a stop-loss order (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."
do_3 = "ShareTokenCreated and TokenRegistered decode into perps.spot_token_registry; Transfer and Approval at a share pointer decode into perps.spot_share_transfers with share_token the emitter and token resolved from the pointer set, a Transfer from or to the zero address being a mint with account to or a burn with account from, and a pointer log whose token cannot be resolved goes to raw_logs with failure_class share_lookup (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."
do_4 = "pricefeed.go registers FeedKeyRegistered and FeedKeyRevoked at 0x1020 from the leaf ABI package precompiles/pricefeed/abi, and decodes each pricefeed_aggregate and pricefeed_aggregate_skipped of the finalize_block_events that Comet returns into one perps.index_prices row with receipt_kind block_event, tx_index -1, log_index its position, tx_hash the block hash and emitter 0x1020, basis signed; the other pricefeed Cosmos events are not decoded (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."
do_5 = "usdl.go declares the ERC20 Transfer event and decodes the Transfer logs of the USDL contract 0x85FcD13735F4309833A503EE804ea32395851479 whose from or to is the perps module EVM address or the spot module EVM address (contracts/address-table.md, module accounts) into perps.usdl_transfers with kind in when the custody address receives and out when it sends and venue that custody address; other USDL transfers are not stored (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."
do_6 = "Add TestDecoderColumnsMatchABI in decode/abi_test.go checking every row of the decoding table against the leaf ABI files (name, argument order, types, indexed flags) and asserting that go list -deps of internal/decode names no precompiles package other than the three abi packages and no modules/lxphost (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."
do_7 = "Add TestSpotDecoders with one subtest per spot and share pointer event plus order_token_lookup, order_token_latest_fallback, order_lookup_failure, order_side, share_pointer_passes, share_mint_burn, fee_events_by_topic and address_set against the node of PERPS_DATA_TEST_RPC; TestPricefeedDecoders with one subtest per pricefeed event plus other_events; and TestUSDLDecoder with subtests Transfer and venue_filter_and_tvl (contracts/data-services.md section 6)."

[capability.7.2.4]
title = "Fact writers in one transaction per block"
reqs = ["7006.1", "7006.2", "7006.3", "7006.4", "7006.5"]
touches = ["platform/perps-data/internal/store/facts.go", "platform/perps-data/internal/store/facts_test.go"]
tests = ["platform/perps-data/internal/store/facts_test.go"]
verification_contract = "go test -count=1 ./platform/perps-data/internal/store/ -run 'TestFactWriters'"
do_1 = "Add store.WriteBlock(ctx, tx, block, rows) that inserts the perps.blocks row, every decoded fact row and every raw_logs row of the block and advances perps.cursors, in the order of CommitCanonical (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/store/canonical.go:66) and under the single-writer lease of AcquireLease (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/store/canonical.go:257) (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."
do_2 = "Inserts use ON CONFLICT (tx_hash, log_index, sub) DO NOTHING, so a block written twice leaves one row per log and sub and the second write changes nothing (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."
do_3 = "Every decoded row also lands in perps.protocol_events (event_name, market_id, args jsonb), and every log or block event that maps to an explorer action lands in perps.tx_actions by the action mapping of contracts/data-services.md section 16, including one Oracle Updated row per block with pricefeed_aggregate events keyed at the first aggregate and one Sealed Batch Executed row per end-block receipt; the watermark read of GetCanonicalWatermark (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/store/canonical.go:453) becomes store.Cursor."
do_4 = "Each fact row is enqueued on the outbox in the same transaction through delivery.Store.Enqueue (Launch-x:shared/delivery/store.go:137), so a row exists in Postgres if and only if its message is pending or published (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."
do_5 = "Add TestFactWriters with subtests one_row_per_log, duplicate_block_noop, outbox_in_same_tx, cursor_advances and lease_refuses_second_writer against PERPS_DATA_TEST_DATABASE_URL (contracts/data-services.md section 5)."

